# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""Encyclopedia descriptions, batch N (DeepSeek)."""
DESC_N = {
    'PT:DSC2': {
        211: "Shinn Asuka is a mobile suit pilot assigned to the Minerva. He is 16 years old. Born and raised in Orb, he lived peacefully with his family, knowing nothing of war. However, during the Earth Alliance invasion of Orb in the previous war, he lost both his parents and his sister before his very eyes. Shortly thereafter, at Todaka's urging, he emigrated to PLANT, and believing that 'power is necessary to protect what is precious,' he joined ZAFT. He graduated from the academy with excellent results and earned the right to wear the red uniform, the mark of an elite pilot. Given this background, while he is cheerful at heart, he has a very sensitive side that can manifest as strong aggression.\nDuraldul, perhaps seeing promise in his hidden potential, chose him as the pilot of the Impulse Gundam, the latest model. When the three second-stage Gundams were stolen, he sortied to take them back. Initially, due to a lack of combat experience, he achieved little, but his repeated exposure to battle and death eventually caused him to awaken SEED. From then on, he fought with remarkable skill and grew into a top ace. While he respected Athrun, he often vented his anger at Athrun's indecisive attitude.\nHis chance encounter with Stella, and their reunion in battle, led him to see in her the image of his late sister. When Stella was taken prisoner, he risked his own safety to help her escape, but she could not escape her cruel fate. When he met Stella again after she lost her memories due to re-adjustment, he tried to persuade her and restore her heart, but his wish went unfulfilled, and she died. Consumed by anger and hatred, he shot down Kira, who had delivered the killing blow to Stella, and also shot down Athrun, who had defected from Durandal. This became the catalyst for him being given the Destiny Gundam and appointed as a member of the special forces FAITH, steadily turning him into Durandal's vanguard.\nDuring the final battle, he listened to Athrun's persuasion but stubbornly continued to fight. In his frenzy, he nearly attacked even Lunamaria, with whom he had shared a connection, but at the last moment he was shot down by Athrun and reunited with Stella in a vision. He awoke on Lunamaria's lap, shedding tears as the war came to its end.\nIn the epilogue added in 'Final Plus,' he visits the memorial in Orb and meets Kira for the second time. They shake hands, vowing to continue fighting together to maintain peace.",
        212: "Ray Za Barrel is a mobile suit pilot assigned to the Minerva. Always calm and possessing excellent situational awareness, his mobile suit piloting skills surpass those of his peers Shinn and Lunamaria. In space, he fought on equal footing with Neo, and his abilities were so highly regarded by those around him that Arthur wondered why Shinn, not Ray, had been chosen to pilot the Impulse. He adores Durandal like a father, and his trust in him is so deep that his personality transforms into that of an innocent boy in Durandal's presence. For this reason, he views the Archangel, which defies Durandal, as an enemy, and his conflict with Athrun, who cannot sever his past ties with them, deepens. When Athrun attempted to desert ZAFT, Ray pulled the trigger without hesitation, intending to kill both him and Meyrin, who had aided his escape. When that failed, he immediately boarded the Legend Gundam and gave chase. He also guided the hesitant Shinn, manipulating him into shooting down Athrun. In truth, like Rau Le Creuset, who died in the previous war, Ray is a clone of Al Da Flaga. He shares the same short telomeres, meaning he was not destined to live long. During the final battle, he was defeated by Kira and his mobile suit was wrecked. He barely managed to reach Durandal inside Messiah, but for the sake of the 'future' Kira spoke of, he fired a bullet at the Durandal he loved and revered. In his final moments, held by Talia, he wept, finally finding a motherly presence, and was consumed by the explosion.",
        213: "Lunamaria Hawke is a mobile suit pilot serving aboard the Minerva in the ZAFT forces. She is 17 years old. Along with Shinn and Ray, she achieved excellent results at the academy and became one of the elite, known as the Red Coats. She primarily fought in a GOUF Ignited painted in her personal color, red. Along with her younger sister Meyrin, she was interested in Athrun, a hero of the previous war, and made various advances toward him. But when she heard that Athrun had deserted the military due to distrust of Durandal, and that Meyrin had gone with him, she was shocked, only to then learn that the two had been shot down. From then on, her bond with Shinn, who supported her as they healed each other's wounds, quickly deepened and eventually blossomed into love. During the final battle, she tried to stop Shinn, who seemed possessed in his determination to keep fighting, but was instead attacked by him. Even so, she showed her devotion by tending to Shinn after his defeat by Athrun. In a post-war scene in 'Final Plus,' she visits the Orb memorial with Shinn. There, she watches Shinn shed tears as he reconciles with Kira and Athrun, and together they step forward into a new future.",
        214: "Talia Gladys is the captain of the newly built ZAFT warship Minerva. She is 29 years old. Living up to her rare status as a female captain in ZAFT, she possesses excellent situational judgment and the ability to command her crew's loyalty, skillfully leading the young crew including Shinn. She was once in a romantic relationship with Durandal, but because she could not bear his child due to compatibility issues, she reluctantly ended their relationship. However, it seems they still harbor unresolved feelings for each other. From the time of the LOGOS subjugation onward, she grew increasingly distrustful of the unreasonable orders and inexplicable actions coming from Durandal. During the final battle, when the Minerva became unable to fight, she entrusted the crew to Arthur and evacuated the ship, heading to Durandal's location to stop him. When he fell after a final exchange with Kira and the others, she watched over his final moments and vanished with him in the explosion of Messiah.",
        215: 'Arthur Trine is the deputy captain of the newly built ZAFT warship Minerva. He is 26 years old. Despite holding the important post of deputy captain, he is timid and restless. He tends to get carried away and was often scolded by Talia. He treated long-serving crew members like Shinn and Ray with familiarity, but often cast a cold eye on Athrun, who joined later. During the final battle at Messiah, when the Minerva was rendered combat-ineffective, Talia entrusted him with full command of the Minerva crew as she headed to Durandal. Gone was the unreliable Arthur of before, as he saluted Talia as she departed.',
        216: "Meyrin was a crew member of the ZAFT new warship Minerva, in charge of communications control and search operations. She was 16 years old.\nAlong with her older sister Lunamaria, she took an interest in Athrun, a hero of the previous war. She was also skilled at operating information terminals, and had used that skill to investigate Athrun's background.\nAs she watched Athrun become increasingly isolated within the ship, she came to feel complex emotions that went beyond mere admiration. When Athrun deserted the military, she assisted him, and carried by the momentum, she chose to accompany him. Although she was shot down by Shinn immediately after their escape, she survived, and from then on followed Athrun and came to belong to the Orb military. Eventually she boarded the Eternal, and supported Lacus with her skilled communications control.\nIn the epilogue added in 'Final Plus,' she appeared before the Orb memorial site alongside Athrun, and walked off side by side with him.",
        217: 'Yolant was a mechanic on the Minerva. He was 17 years old.\nHe was a classmate and friend of Ray and Meyrin from the academy.\nUnlike his partner Vino, he had a serious personality. As a big Lacus fan, he was jealous of Athrun, who was publicly her fiance. At one point he made remarks, half joking and half serious, about pulling the plug on the Saber.',
        218: 'Vino was a mechanic on the Minerva. He was 16 years old.\nHe was a classmate and friend of Shinn and Lunamaria from the academy.\nUnlike his partner Yolant, he had a light and cheerful personality. He had been especially close to Shinn, so when Meyrin fled with Athrun and Shinn pursued and shot them down, Vino harbored complicated feelings toward him.',
        219: 'Alex Dino was the alias Athrun used when he defected to Orb after the end of the previous war.\nWhen going out, he wore no disguise beyond sunglasses, so it is not hard to imagine that anyone who knew him would see through it at a glance. In fact, Durandal saw through it immediately.',
        220: "Athrun was one of the key figures who brought the previous war to an end, and a hero whose name was known by everyone in PLANT. He was 18 years old.\nAfter the war, he defected to Orb and served as the bodyguard of his lover Cagalli. But before the war that began anew, he was forced to taste the powerlessness of being unable to do anything. In that state, Durandal invited him, and after bidding Cagalli farewell, he rejoined ZAFT. He became a member of the special forces unit FAITH.\nHe piloted the Saber Gundam entrusted to him upon rejoining and fought as a crew member of the Minerva, but eventually came into conflict with Kira and the others due to differences in opinion.\nInitially he sympathized with Durandal's ideals, but as he received suspicions of Lacus's assassination, the use of the fake Meer, and orders to attack the Archangel whose aims should have been the same, he gradually grew more distrustful.\nHowever, his indecisive attitude caused Durandal to see him as a threat. When he was about to be disposed of, he narrowly escaped with advice from Meer and aid from Meyrin, and attempted to desert the military again. But he was pursued by Shinn and Ray, and was shot down along with Meyrin, who was with him.",
        221: "Athrun Zala, who escaped from ZAFT and decided to fight alongside Kira and the others once more. To stand against Durandal's 'Destiny Plan', he formally became a member of the Orb military. The hesitation he once felt when caught between what he believed in and what he wanted to believe in is already gone. Moreover, by obtaining the Infinite Justice Gundam, which carries on the lineage of his beloved former mobile suit, he was able to fully display his true combat ability. During the final battle, he attempted to persuade Shinn, who was following Durandal, to stop fighting, but failed. When the deranged Shinn showed signs of attacking Lunamaria, who had intervened to stop him, Athrun activated SEED and shot him down. In 'Final Plus', he further pursued Kira to Messiah, where Durandal awaited, and witnessed the end of the battle. After the war, standing beside Athrun at the Orb memorial monument was not Cagalli but Meyrin. Athrun has a reputation for getting into trouble involving women, so it is unclear whether she has truly been decided as his partner...",
        222: "A crew member of the Archangel and pilot of the Freedom Gundam. Eighteen years old. An existence that could be called a 'Super Coordinator', born through genetic adjustment and a variety of repeated experiments. During the previous war, he fought as a third force against both the Earth Alliance and PLANT, leading the war to its conclusion. Afterwards, he defected to Orb along with Murrue, with whom he had fought, and his lover Lacus. He lived in seclusion in a world far from battle. However, upon witnessing the Junius Seven drop incident, and triggered by a battle against an assassination squad sent after Lacus, he began to strongly feel the need to halt the spreading flames of war. And at last, he commenced military action together with his former comrades. His combat ability is so high that no one can match him. Yet because of his overly gentle personality, which abhors conflict and killing, he strives to fight in a way that destroys only weapons and cameras, avoiding killing his opponents. This eventually became his undoing, and he was once defeated by Shinn's desperate attack. But later, he achieved a revival by obtaining new wings, the Strike Freedom Gundam. After Durandal revealed the existence of the 'Destiny Plan', he formally joined the Orb military following Cagalli's return to the position of representative chief. In the final battle, he settled his score with Ray, who carried on the lingering ties of Rau Le Creuset, then infiltrated Messiah to confront Durandal, showing his resolve to keep fighting in a troubled world.",
        223: "The representative of the Orb Union of Chief States. Eighteen years old. She carries on the will of the former representative Uzumi, striving to lead her homeland and the world to peace. However, due to her youth, inexperience, and the behind-the-scenes machinations of the Seiran father and son, the nation failed to unite, and she keenly felt her own powerlessness. When Athrun, with whom she had been in a romantic relationship since the previous war, left Orb, he gave her a ring. But afterwards, for the reason of 'uniting the nation', she reluctantly decided to marry Yuna, cutting off her feelings. However, during the wedding ceremony, she was carried off by the Freedom Gundam of her twin brother Kira, and the marriage fell apart. Afterward, the Seiran family, who had seized real power, began to move the military by allying with the Earth Alliance, and she tried to stop them but failed. Yet witnessing the desperate resolve of the Orb military men renewed her determination to protect her homeland. When a crisis later befell Orb, she rode the Akatsuki left by Uzumi, returned to her country, and saved it from danger. After regaining her position as Orb's representative, she governed the nation well and stood against Durandal, who proposed the 'Destiny Plan'. Perhaps to prove that resolve, she removed the ring given to her by Athrun, entrusting his well-being to Meyrin.",
        224: "The captain of the Archangel. Twenty-eight years old. For convenience, her rank was that of lieutenant commander from her Earth Alliance days, but after formally becoming a member of the Orb military, her rank became that of colonel. During the previous war, she originally belonged to the Earth Alliance military, but came to question the military's actions and defected midway. As a third force, she became the driving force that led the previous war to its conclusion. Though she sometimes makes cold-blooded decisions, she is by nature a kind-hearted woman who has watched over her young crew like a mother. After the war ended, she crossed to Orb with Kira, Waltfeld, Lacus, and others who had fought alongside her, and worked in the shipbuilding section of Morgenroete, Inc. Just as she was considering moving to PLANT, she was attacked by a special forces unit plotting to assassinate Lacus, but barely managed to repel them. With that incident as the catalyst, she resolved to launch the Archangel once more for the sake of a world again descending into chaos. During the battle in Berlin, she was reunited with her lover Mu, who was supposed to have died shielding the Archangel in the previous war, but he had lost all his memories. In her heartache, she told him to leave the ship, but Mu, feeling something nagging at his heart, came back. And as if drawn to each other, the two opened their hearts to one another. During the final battle, Mu once again became the shield of the Archangel. But this time he survived along with his machine, and moreover had completely regained his memories. Witnessing this miracle, she shed tears of joy.",
        225: 'The helmsman of the Archangel. Twenty-seven years old. His nominal rank is that of ensign from his Earth Alliance days. After being formally incorporated into the Orb military, his rank became that of lieutenant. After the previous war, he apparently lived as an ordinary citizen of Orb. Even so, whether navigating on land, under water, or in space, or performing evasive maneuvers during combat, he skillfully piloted the Archangel in all times and places, demonstrating that his skill remained intact. The fact that he could fight on equal terms or better against the new ship Minerva was largely due to his helmsmanship. He may have had feelings for Miriallia, as he looked quite displeased when Chandra appeared during their conversation. But of course, what happened afterward remains unknown.',
        226: "Chandra is the Archangel's controller, responsible for search, radar, and fire control. He is 26 years old. For convenience, his rank was set as Sergeant First Class from his days in the Earth Alliance, but after formally becoming a member of the Orb military, he holds the rank of Second Lieutenant. His whereabouts after the previous war were unknown, and as can be seen from the lack of a return scene, he casts a weak shadow other than his name. However, he performs his duties reliably, and in the understaffed Archangel, which struggles with a shortage of personnel greater than in the previous war, he is an indispensable presence. Regarding Miriallia, upon his return he showed signs of interest, such as being the first to confirm her relationship with Dearka and interrupting a chat between her and Neumann. However, what happened afterward is likewise unknown.",
        227: "Miriallia is a member of the Archangel's crew responsible for communications control. She is 18 years old. Originally nothing more than an ordinary student, she was drawn into the military in the previous war. Having lost her lover Tolle on the battlefield, she was for a time consumed by a dark hatred of Coordinators. But as she learned of the war's hidden truths, she grew emotionally and fought through to the war's end. After the war, she worked as a battlefield journalist, photographing and witnessing wars around the world with camera in hand. Combined with her own past experiences, she grieved for a world stained by conflict, but when the Archangel launched, she boarded again to fight alongside them. Regarding Dearka, who had harbored unrequited feelings for her, things apparently did not work out. When she happened to run into Athrun on a street corner and chatted with him, she visibly grimaced at the mention of Dearka's name, suggesting that there was some decisive factor in why the two never became lovers.",
        228: "Lacus was once called the 'Songstress of PLANT' and is an idol-like figure. She is 18 years old. Her presence and charisma are immense, and in the previous war she guided the paths of Kira and Athrun, gathered those who shared her ideals, and was a major driving force in bringing the conflict to an end. After the previous war, she went to Orb with Waltfeld, Murrue, and her lover Kira, who had fought alongside her. There she lived quietly with Reverend Malchio, Kira's adoptive mother Carida, and orphans, but her brief peace was shattered by the appearance of those who sought to assassinate her. With the emergence of the impostor Meer, her suspicions of Durandal deepened. Resolving to return to the public stage, she boarded the Archangel with Kira. Later, going into space and learning of the 'Destiny Plan,' she declared her opposition to it. When she prepared new Gundams for Kira and Athrun, she personally boarded the Infinite Justice Gundam (though she mostly just rode along) and delivered it to Athrun. She also worked energetically, gathering forces from various quarters, and became the ideological pillar for those who opposed Durandal. In the final battle, as in the previous war, she boarded the Eternal and stood at the front lines, fulfilling her role as a standard-bearer. After the fight with Durandal, she was seen at Kira's side in both public and private matters.",
        230: "Dakosta is Waltfeld's adjutant. In the previous war he belonged to ZAFT, but he defected with Waltfeld and joined the Clyne faction. In place of his superior, he always works behind the scenes, faithfully carrying out his duties. In the current war as well, he plays a fairly important role, such as guarding the Eternal while Lacus and the others were away, and discovering notes about the Destiny Plan within the abandoned colony Mendel. On that occasion, he was followed by a ZAFT reconnaissance unit and nearly brought about a critical situation that could have led to the ship's sinking.",
        231: "Mudock is the Archangel's chief mechanic. He is 33 years old. For convenience, his rank was set as Sergeant Major from his Earth Alliance days, but his rank after formally being incorporated into the Orb military is unknown. After the previous war, he apparently worked at Morgenroete and handles all maintenance for both mobile suits and the Archangel, making his undiminished skill understandable. He is stubborn and foul-mouthed, and his appearance gives a rough impression. But his sense of responsibility toward his position as a mechanic, whose work affects pilots' lives, and the feelings for his comrades that stem from it, are stronger than most. When Athrun tried to sortie despite his injury, he contacted Murrue to have her stop him. Also, right after Mu (Neo) returned, he was seen smiling happily.",
        232: "Yuna Roma Seiran was the heir of the Seiran family, one of the five great clans of Orb, and the fiance of Cagalli. He was 22 years old.\nCollaborating with his father Unato, he skillfully manipulated words to carry out his marriage to Cagalli, aiming to take control of Orb in name and in fact. During the wedding ceremony that eventually took place, Cagalli was taken from him by Kira's Freedom Gundam. He was further interrupted in subsequent battles against the Minerva, and his pride was thoroughly crushed each time.\nAfter Cagalli's absence allowed him to assume the seat of Orb's representative, he went to the front lines as the commander leading the Orb fleet. However, his command ability was utterly nonexistent, being nothing short of clumsy. He obsessed over operation names to the point of boring those around him, and slept soundly alone while other crew members worked through the night, making his frivolous attitude plainly visible.\nIn reality, he had connections with LOGOS behind the scenes, and secretly sheltered Djibril when he was forced to flee. Because he refused to hand Djibril over even after being found out, Orb came under a full-scale attack from ZAFT. When Cagalli eventually returned, he forgot that he had denounced her as a fake and tried to ingratiate himself with her, but was promptly arrested for high treason. He attempted to escape in the confusion of battle after being deposed, but was crushed to death by a GOUF that happened to fall on him.",
        233: 'Unato Emma Seiran was the head of the Seiran family, one of the five great clans of Orb, and the father of Yuna.\nWhile holding the position of chancellor supporting the nation, he plotted to dominate Orb by having Yuna marry Cagalli.\nBehind the scenes, he was deeply involved with LOGOS, and because he sheltered the fleeing Djibril, Orb came under a full-scale attack from ZAFT. Eventually, the shelter where he had taken refuge came under attack, and he met his end buried under the rubble.',
        234: "Todaka was the captain of the aircraft carrier Takemikazuchi belonging to the Orb Navy. His rank was Captain (Colonel).\nHe had a warm-hearted personality and sound judgment, and enjoyed the deep trust of his subordinates.\nHe constantly harbored resentment toward unreasonable orders, such as attacks on the Minerva, which had saved Earth from the fall of Junius Seven, and on the Archangel, which carried Cagalli, the head of state. When Yuna, who had boarded the ship as supreme commander, issued the reckless order to 'attack that Cagalli as she is a fake,' he judged that, having formed an alliance with the Earth Alliance, it was unavoidable in order to protect Orb. Placing his hopes on the Freedom Gundam to serve as escort, he gave the order to attack with great reluctance.\nIn the battle off the coast of Crete, seeing that the outcome was decided, he barked at his subordinates and ordered them to go to the Archangel. Then, aboard the sinking ship, he was cut in two along with the bridge by Shinn's Sword Impulse. His conduct, remaining faithful to his duty as an Orb soldier to the very end, truly embodied the ideals that Orb upheld. Incidentally, it was Todaka who had arranged for Shinn's family to relocate to PLANT after he lost them, but the two who faced each other in battle had no way of knowing of each other's existence.",
        235: "Rednil Kisaka was a soldier belonging to the Orb Army. His rank was Captain (Colonel).\nHe was a direct subordinate of Uzumi, the former head of state of Orb, and had served as Cagalli's guard during the previous war. After Uzumi's death, he continued to watch over Cagalli as her guardian.\nAfter the alliance between the Earth Alliance and Orb, he infiltrated the Earth Alliance forces to probe their movements. Along the way, when he learned of Athrun and Meyrin's escape, he rescued them after they had been shot down and guided them to the Archangel.\nWhen Cagalli insisted on sortieing upon learning of Orb's crisis, he entrusted her with the Akatsuki that Uzumi had left behind. He himself also sortied in a Murasame.",
        236: "Gilbert Durandal was the Chairman of the PLANT Supreme Council. He was 32 years old.\nUnlike the previous chairman, Patrick Zara, he was a moderate who sought a path of coexistence and peace with the Naturals. During the Junius Seven fall incident and the subsequent battles with the Earth Alliance forces, he consistently made calm and precise decisions, demonstrating excellent leadership.\nHe was also an authority on genetic research, and it is believed that he came to know Kruze and Ray through that connection. There were also signs that he had anticipated from the beginning that Shinn would manifest SEED.\nHe propped up Meer as Lacus, attempting to boost the fighting spirit of all of PLANT. However, his secret plot to assassinate the real Lacus was exposed, drawing the opposition of Kira and the others.\nHis ultimate goal was to construct a managed society that controlled humanity at the genetic level, which he called the 'Destiny Plan.' After destroying LOGOS, he declared the introduction and implementation of the plan to the world, but was stopped by Kira and the others, who rejected a world where evolution had ceased.\nIn the end, he was shot by Ray, whom he had trusted like his own son. And so, his life came to a close in the lap of Talia, who had once been his lover and had continued to hold feelings for him even after their separation.",
        237: "Yzak Joule is captain of the ZAFT Joule Team. Age 19.\nIn the previous war, at the very end, he cooperated with the Archangel and the Eternal, and together they helped bring about the war's conclusion.\nAfter the war ended, with Durandal's assistance, he returned to ZAFT, and thanks to his talents, he rose at a young age to the position of team captain. His ability to command his unit through abundant combat experience, and his skill in battle, are first-rate. He was active on a wide scale in space: helping to stop the fall of Junius Seven in cooperation with the Minerva, defending PLANT from the Earth Alliance's one-sided attacks, and attempting to destroy the beam deflection station when PLANT became a target of Requiem (though that attempt ended in failure).\nWhen he met Athrun again, he strongly urged him to re-enlist, showing that he had outgrown the petty rivalries he once clung to and had matured.\nDuring the final battle between Orb and PLANT, he once again found himself torn between a friend who had become an enemy and his own position. However, he opposed Durandal, who used weapons of mass destruction like Requiem and Neo Genesis, and once again cooperated with Kira and the others.\nAfter successfully destroying the beam deflection station for the second time, he took up defense of the Eternal. His justification for doing so was, characteristically for Yzak, a forceful one.",
        238: "A member of ZAFT, serving as adjutant under his best friend Yzak in the Joule Team. Age 19.\nHe belonged to ZAFT in the previous war as well, but after being taken prisoner, he boarded the Archangel and fought alongside it. After contributing as a third faction to ending the war, he returned to PLANT.\nIt is not certain whether it was because of that incident, but he now wears the uniform of a regular soldier rather than the red coat of an elite. However, his skill as a pilot is in no way diminished, and it can be said he has grown into a more reliable man, mentally as well.\nIt was thought he might develop a good relationship with Miriallia, for whom he had developed feelings, but she herself confirmed with her own mouth that she had 'dumped him.'",
        239: "A member of ZAFT's special forces unit FAITH. Transferred to the Minerva by Durandal's order. Age 21.\nBright and easygoing, he possessed the adaptability and sociability to blend into the Minerva's crew immediately despite joining mid-mission. He was especially attentive to Athrun, admonishing him when he saw him troubled over battle, and working to close the distance between Athrun and the guarded Shinn and the others.\nHis mobile suit piloting skill was also high, and his machine was always painted in his personal color orange. At the PLANT defense battle he fought in a ZAKU Phantom, and at the Dardanelles Strait he was active in an early-deployed GOUF Ignited. However, when the Freedom Gundam intruded to stop the battle and deprived him of his combat capability, he was attacked from behind by the Gaia Gundam and cut in two along with his machine, dying.\nIncidentally, in German, 'Westen' means 'west' and 'flus' means 'river'. This is a name chosen out of respect for Heine's voice actor, who also performed the theme song: the artist Nishikawa Takanori.",
        240: "A girl sought out by Durandal, who thought that after Lacus vanished from public view, someone was needed to draw the people's hearts as her substitute. Age 17.\nBeing herself a great fan of Lacus, her appearance appealing for peace moved many hearts, and her singing voice attracted many people. Having undergone plastic surgery, her appearance and voice were exactly the same as the genuine article's. However, because her song arrangements and mannerisms were quite different, Yolant and others regarded her with some suspicion. Even so, in the end she seems to have gained popularity approaching the real thing.\nWhether out of a faithful attempt to uphold the fiction that she was engaged to Athrun, or out of genuine affection, she made excessive advances toward him, much to his bewilderment. When she learned that danger was approaching Athrun, she secretly informed him and saved him from the crisis. At that time, when he extended his hand to flee together, she struck it away, declaring, 'Even as a fake, I want to be Lacus.'\nLater, her unstable mental state - fearing she was no longer needed - was exploited by an attendant under Durandal's command, who manipulated her into having the real Lacus killed. However, Lacus's words made her realize her error, and she shielded Lacus with her body from assassins' bullets, breathing her last in Lacus's arms.",
        241: "A member of the military-industrial complex LOGOS and the new leader of Blue Cosmos, which seeks the extermination of Coordinators. Age 31.\nA man of excessive aristocratic tastes and twisted elitist ideology. Ordinarily he maintains a calm and courteous demeanor, but when matters do not go as planned he quickly loses his temper and lashes out at things around him - a base character.\nWhen he learned that the Junius Seven drop was the work of certain Coordinators, he used it as justification to unilaterally declare war against PLANT, plunging the world into chaos once more.\nHowever, both he and LOGOS itself were exposed by Durandal's machinations, and he became the sole target of the people's hostility. Thereafter he suffered defeats one after another across the world, fleeing while using everyone else - LOGOS members, Earth Alliance officers, all - as stepping stones. Even at Daedalus Base on the Moon, his last stronghold, he was defeated, and though recovery was impossible he still attempted escape. But he was shot through along with the bridge of the Girty Lue he had boarded, and with his death the flight came to an end.",
        242: "Neo Roanoke was the captain of the Earth Alliance's 81st Independent Mobile Group, the Phantom Pain. His rank was colonel. He was a man of many mysteries, always hiding his face behind a mask and having an unknown history. Despite his carefree personality, his command and combat abilities were high, and his approachable and considerate nature earned him the deep trust of his subordinates. Beyond his unmilitary-like personality, he possessed many traits that called to mind Mwu La Flaga, who had died in the previous war, such as his high spatial awareness that allowed him to freely manipulate GUNBARRELs, and an ability to sense the presence of another person that manifested between him and Ray. He engaged Kira in battle over Berlin and was shot down, and when he was thrown from the cockpit, his unveiled face was exactly that of Mwu. Examination revealed his biological data to be identical, confirming him to be Mwu La Flaga himself. Afterward, he was held as a prisoner aboard the Archangel, but was released by the hand of Murrue, his former lover. However, from the faint remnants of his past memories and fragments of his feelings for Murrue, he decided to return to the ship and fight alongside them. Later, when he was formally incorporated into the Orb military, he became the pilot of the Akatsuki in place of Cagalli, who had to remain on Earth, and achieved great results in battle. His rank remained that of a colonel, and even considering that he was a man who had been with the enemy until shortly before, was an acquaintance, and was skilled, the generous treatment he received was truly exceptional.",
        244: "Sting Oakley was an Extended belonging to the Earth Alliance special forces unit Phantom Pain. He stole the Chaos Gundam from ZAFT and became its pilot. For these Extendeds, a verbal safety device called a 'Block Word' was prepared to suppress their rampages. Upon hearing that word, they would immediately fall into a state of confusion and lose themselves. However, Sting's 'Block Word' was never revealed. Compared to Auel and Stella, he was the most mentally stable, and he was earnest in his duties and obediently followed orders, making him the leader among the three. In a battle over the streets of Berlin, he engaged the spirited Orb Murasame units and was shot down without being able to retreat. He was thought to have died there, but later returned to the front lines as the pilot of the Destroy Gundam. However, he had been transformed into a biological CPU with further enhancements and adjustments, and his personality had become pathologically bloodthirsty. In the end, he was struck down by Shinn, who was burning with rage at his brutal fighting.",
        245: "Auel Neider was an Extended belonging to the Earth Alliance special forces unit Phantom Pain. He stole the Abyss Gundam from ZAFT and became its pilot. True to his youthful appearance, he was capricious and free-spirited like a boy. He would casually hurl abuse at his superior, Neo, ignore withdrawal orders to achieve results, and showed numerous problems in his words and actions. For these Extendeds, a verbal safety device called a 'Block Word' was prepared to suppress their rampages. Upon hearing that word, they would fall into a state of confusion and lose themselves. In Auel's case, the word was 'Mother', and he once fell into a state of confusion due to his own utterance of that word. He engaged Shinn's Blast Impulse, which had manifested SEED, and in a brief opening created by using the explosion of the Silhouette as a distraction, his cockpit was pierced by a beam javelin, and he vanished into the sea.",
        246: "Stella Loussier was an Extended belonging to the Earth Alliance special forces unit Phantom Pain. She stole the Gaia Gundam from ZAFT and became its pilot. For these Extendeds, a verbal safety device called a 'Block Word' was prepared to suppress their rampages. Upon hearing that word, they would immediately fall into a state of confusion and lose themselves. In Stella's case, the word was 'Death', and she would frequently hear it and fall into a state of confusion. Compared to Sting and Auel, she was the most mentally unstable. In normal times she was timid and quiet, but in combat she revealed a ferocious destructive impulse. Whether her obedient following of Neo's orders in any state was due to such adjustments or personal feelings remains unknown. She reacted to Auel's words 'Mother is going to die' and, as if to deny them, sortied alone. She was defeated and taken prisoner by the Minerva, but escaped danger through the hand of Shinn, who was an acquaintance. Stella was returned on the condition that she not be involved in battle from then on, but peaceful times did not come to her. Eventually, she was adjusted once more and, having lost her memories, was made the pilot of the Destroy Gundam. With overwhelming destructive power, she burned the city of Berlin, its inhabitants, and the garrison forces to ashes. She briefly regained her composure through Shinn's persuasion, but upon seeing the Freedom Gundam in her sight, she fell into a frenzy. As she was about to fire her beam as if to wipe everything out, she was stopped by Kira and consumed by the explosion of her cockpit. In her final moment, she regained her memories and smiled, and fell into an eternal sleep while watched over by Shinn.",
        247: "Ian Lee was a soldier belonging to the Earth Alliance special forces unit Phantom Pain. His rank was lieutenant colonel. He served as captain of the Girty Lue, the new vessel that served as the unit's mother ship, and was a capable commander who could make cool and accurate judgments. However, after his superior Neo's area of activity moved to the ground, he was no longer seen. He appeared again briefly when Djibril escaped from the Daedalus base on the Moon, but was blown away along with the bridge by Ray, and was never to be seen again.",
        249: "Sato is a former ZAFT soldier who deserted and now leads a terrorist unit. Their group is made up of those who lost loved ones in the war. As such, they harbor intense rage not only toward Naturals, but also toward Coordinators who enjoy a false peace. Believing that Patrick Zala's hardline approach was the correct path for vengeance and reform, he plotted to drop Junius Seven onto Earth.\nAs a veteran, his skills were formidable; despite piloting the outdated ZIN High Maneuver Type 2, he consistently overwhelmed the superior-spec Gates R and fought on par with or better than the new ZAKU. However, before the might of veterans who had fought through the previous war, such as Yzak, his comrades were gradually whittled down.\nIn the end, he tried to take Athrun with him, but was blocked by Shinn and slammed into the surface of Junius Seven, where he exploded and died.",
        250: 'Baba is the captain of a Murasame unit belonging to the Orb forces. His rank is First Lieutenant (Captain). In the battle off the coast of Crete, he received a ceasefire order from Cagalli, but continued to fight to protect his homeland. He then launched a suicide attack on the bow of the Minerva and exploded along with his machine.',
        251: "Joseph Copeland is the president of the Atlantic Federation, one of the powerful nations belonging to the Earth Alliance. On the surface he is the supreme leader of the Earth Alliance, but in reality he is a puppet of LOGOS, and was forced by its leader, Djibril, to decide on opening hostilities with PLANT. When Requiem was fired at the Earth Alliance base Alzachel on Durandal's orders, he happened to be present and was obliterated along with the base.",
        252: "Gainer Sanga is an ordinary seventeen-year-old boy living in Ugrusk, notable only for his skill at games. His parents were killed by Exodusists, leaving him with a deep-seated hatred of the Exodus and a psychological scar that drove him into seclusion. Immersing himself in the online game 'Overman Battle', he eventually achieved 200 consecutive victories and earned the champion title of 'King'.\nOne day, in a prison where he was held on false charges, he met Gain and hitched onto the prison break. Along the way, he obtained an Overman, which he named 'King Gainer', and showed off his game champion skills against the pursuing Siberian Railway guards. Thus, he ended up participating in the Exodus almost by default.\nDue to his past experiences, he was initially quite introverted. But through fighting amidst a swirl of emotions - admiration for and rebellion against Gain, feelings for Sara, his own responsibilities and potential - he continued to battle, and the ceiling of Yapan became a great source of strength for continuing the Exodus. At the same time, he grew as a person.\nIn a battle against Cynthia, his game rival and a subordinate of Kids Munt, he lost without being able to fight seriously and was gravely wounded. However, Cynthia was also shocked by the real combat where blood was actually spilled, and that opening led to her being captured by the Overdevil.\nTo save Cynthia, he undertook special training to face both his game rival and a real enemy simultaneously. After a hard-fought struggle, he achieved victory and succeeded in surpassing his former self. Bearing the new title of 'King', he headed to Cynthia, and although he was absorbed by the Overdevil along the way, he succeeded in freeing her with the support of Sara and Gain.",
        253: "Gain Bijou is an Exodus contractor who designs the Ugrusk Exodus. He is 28 years old. He is a master sniper whose shots from his beloved sniper rifle 'Angerma Zaisa' always hit their mark. He is known by the epithet 'Black Southern Cross' for carving six cross-shaped bullet scars into his targets, and holds the chivalrous principle of never shooting an opponent who turns his back and flees.\nHe often tries to charm women and says things that may be lies or sincere, so he is often seen as a frivolous man, but in truth he is a principled and loyal person who detests crookedness. Furthermore, he is quick-witted, skilled in hand-to-hand combat, and demonstrates excellent talent in handling silhouette machines and Overmen. He is a reliable man no matter what he does, and those who know his true nature place immense trust in him.\nHis current name is a pseudonym; his real name is 'Charle Felibe'. He was born into the ducal house of Domepolis Ubbus, which was ruined after a failed Exodus. During that failed Exodus, he experienced painful events, including the death of his lover Gaera and witnessing the slaughter among the people of Ubbus. However, by successfully (or in the story, almost successfully) pulling off the Ugrusk Exodus, it seems that his past was at least partially redeemed.",
        254: "Sara Kodama is a classmate of Gainer's whom he secretly harbors feelings for. She is 17 years old. As a member of the Gauli Squad, she fights in a Silhouette Machine with courage, and possesses the strength to frequently scold Gainer and Bello, even holding her own against Adette as a woman. She is a cheerful and bright girl. Her strong sense of independence seems largely due to the fact that she is actually an orphan, and perhaps for that reason, she regarded Gainer as a particularly pathetic man. Even so, as they shared actions during the Exodus and their opportunities to interact increased, she gradually revised her opinion of him. When Gainer confessed his feelings for Sara to counter the Over Skill of Planeta, it resounded throughout the ceiling of Yapan. Sara ran off blushing deeply, and nearly everyone who saw or heard it learned of their relationship. Eventually, when Gainer suffered an Over Freeze, she pressed her lips to his to save him, but she herself ended up in the same state as a result. Then, she became a servant of Cynthia and Gainer, riding Jinba to steal the lives of those on the ceiling of Yapan. However, while being hindered by Martina and Adette, she was restored by the Over Heat of King Gainer. In the end, also under the watch of the people, she and Gainer exchanged their feelings for each other.",
        255: "Bello Corish is a classmate of Gainer's. He is 20 years old. While serving as a member of the Gauli Squad and boarding a Silhouette Machine, he is also in charge of steering the Bach Cron that tows the ceiling of Yapan. Because he repeated a grade, he is older than Gainer and Sara, but despite that, he is a bit of a joker and restless, so he could pass for the same age. However, this personality works in his favor, making him a good partner for the introverted Gainer, and they have built a friendship that could be called close. He has feelings for Sara and always strives to show off his good side. But the Exodus continued without things going well for him, and in the end, Sara ended up on good terms with Gainer. After the battle with the Overdevil, he gave a somewhat desperate round of applause to the two who had exchanged their feelings.",
        256: "Gauli Hughes is the captain of the self-defense group 'Gauli Squad' of Urgusk. He is 28 years old. He masters a suspicious technique called 'Yapan Ninpo,' and his combat abilities, from physical arts (ninjutsu) to piloting Silhouette Machines, are extremely high. Normally, he has a warm and gentle personality, but his true nature is that of an Exodus supremacist. For the sake of carrying out the Exodus, he does not choose his means or ends, and at times he resorts to merciless methods. In fact, it was Gauli who killed Gainer's parents, but he continued to regret that act, harboring a sentimentality that could not fully commit to ruthlessness. Because of this, he feels conflict over his position. He was once taken in by Desnetta due to this weakness being exploited, but was rescued by Gainer, who was inwardly conflicted upon learning the truth. In the final battle against the Overdevil, he was Over Freezed and lost his sentimentality and conflict, becoming an ice demon who sought only to use his combat abilities for destruction and slaughter. However, receiving the desperate kiss of Adette, who was in love with Gauli, he thawed the darkness in his heart.",
        257: "Adette Kistler is a member of the Siberia Railway Guard. She is 25 years old. She has a caring, big-sisterly nature and is respected by Enge and Kejinan as 'Big Sis' and by Jaboli as 'Lady.' She frequently clashed with the people of the ceiling of Yapan, such as fighting Gainer to prevent the Exodus, or infiltrating alone to seize Princess Ana and engaging Gain in hand-to-hand combat. After failing to attack Yassaba and breaking off, she was left behind on the ceiling of Yapan and lost her destination. Later, while participating in events like the sports day, she ended up joining the Exodus by circumstance.",
        258: "Having quit the Siberia Railway, Adette became a teacher at the school Gainer attends. Having arrived at this state by circumstance, she had no place to live and forced her way into Gainer's room as a freeloader. Initially, she caused problems like helping herself to the students' school lunches, but with her innate adaptability, she quickly settled into life on the ceiling of Yapan. 'A clumsy, rough, selfish, truly hopeless person' is how Gainer, who shared bed and board with her, put it. When the people of the dome polis Gangaran established a self-defense group, they were impressed by her combat abilities and selected her as captain, forming the 'Adette Squad.' She stole a Dobeck from the Siberia Railway as her severance pay and equipped her squad with it, and though her methods were the same as ever, she displayed a captaincy befitting her drive and leadership. She is only interested in strong men and provided individual training to toughen up Gainer. During her Siberia Railway days, her interest was in Yassaba, but now it seems to be in Gauli. When Gauli was manipulated by the Over Freeze, she kissed him without regard for the danger and succeeded in restoring his sense of self.",
        259: 'Ana Medaiyu is the daughter of the Medaiyu ducal family of Domepolis Urgusk. She is eight years old. She was taken as a nominal hostage for carrying out the Exodus by Gain and the Gainer that accompanied him. Thanks to her vigorous curiosity, she accompanies the Exodus while enjoying herself.\nWhile she has a guileless personality befitting her age, she sometimes shows adult-like thinking and speech. When taken hostage by Asuham, she criticized his actions with a resolute attitude.\nAfter defeating the Overdevil, she performed the monkey dance familiar from the opening.',
        261: "Mamadou Azaf is the mechanic for the Gauli squad and also a history teacher at the school Gain and the others attend. He is 42 years old. He once served as Gain's tutor, and even now he finds excuses to grumble at him. Also, when the two are alone, he calls Gain by his real name, 'Shalle-sama.'\nEventually he fell in love with Lyubov, who was young enough to be his daughter.",
        262: "Lyubov Smetana is Ana's tutor and caretaker. She is 20 years old. Though she gives an impression of being intelligent and quiet, she does not hesitate to put herself in danger for Ana's sake. Furthermore, when Gain appeared at the Medaiyu residence, she took the initiative to introduce herself, revealing that she is actually an active and bold person.\nShe once fought with Kona over Gain, but in the end she became romantically involved with Mamadou.",
        267: "Miia Lauzin is a singer who bears the same name as the first Miia, one of the Five Sages of legend. She is 20 years old. She enjoys tremendous popularity everywhere, aiming for Japan while singing at the 'Ceiling of Japan' at one time and dancing along the Siberian Railway at another.\nDuring the final battle against the Overdevil, she sang before the King Gainer and sent cheers of support.",
        268: "Lubul Wong Dara is Miia's manager. She is 36 years old. Though considerably older in age, she insists she is from the same generation as Miia.\nShe became the manager because she judged Miia would be a source of money, and she is a commercially shrewd woman who even pitched Miia to the Siberian Railway.\nWhen they reached the Riman coast leading to Japan and Miia ran out into the sea, she scolded her not for the act itself but for getting her costume wet.",
        269: "Medaiyu is Ana's father and the lord of the domed city of Urgusk. He is 51 years old. Known as the 'Art Duke' for the large collection of artworks and furnishings he has gathered in his castle, the King Gainer was one of those pieces. He has a gentle personality, his administration is without problems, and he was beloved by his subjects as a person. When Ana made her first contact after the Exodus and said she intended to return to Urgusk, he showed a father's kindness by disowning her to protect her from danger. When the battle against the Overdevil caused the King Gainer to boil the whole world, he ran out shouting that he would follow Ana in the Exodus.",
        271: "Yassaba Jin is the captain of the Siberian Railway Guard. He is 32 years old. He devotes himself fully to stopping the Exodus and rooting out Exodus sympathizers, and he will use any means to accomplish these goals. However, he is more of a warrior than a soldier by nature, and he sometimes shows a willingness to accept defeat with grace and kindness toward those without power. He repeatedly assaults the 'Ceiling of Yapan,' but each time he is thwarted by the King Gainer and suffers defeat after defeat. He was once taken prisoner but escaped through a gap in the watch, and during his flight he met the fortune-telling girl Eifa. He rescued the girl, who was being mistreated by her master, but he suffered yet another defeat in the battle that followed. With his options exhausted, Yassaba carried out the Exodus together with Eifa. But during their escape they encountered a Golem, and he was struck by gunfire, leaving his fate unknown. Later, however, he was confirmed to be continuing the Exodus with Eifa.",
        272: "Kejinan Dad is a member of the Siberian Railway Guard. He is 31 years old. He has a simple personality: fawning before the strong and being oppressive toward the weak. When his captain Yassaba lost his Overman, he tried to have him killed and claim the captaincy himself, and when he saw himself in a position above Adette, he used the opportunity to press a marriage proposal - his conduct is consistent no matter who he deals with. In a sense, one might say he is a man of steadfast character. After Yassaba vanished and Kashmar died, he lost his superiors one after another and came under the direct command of the Kids. There he obtained a promise, albeit verbal, of a promotion of 46 ranks to become Vice President of the Siberian Railway. It seemed the path to advancement had finally opened, but in the end he had to settle for remaining a 'self-styled' Vice President.",
        273: 'Enge Gam is a member of the Siberian Railway Guard. He is 30 years old. With his fierce looks and eyepatch he gives an impression of toughness, but inside he has a somewhat pessimistic personality. He thinks of himself as number two rather than number one, and he always yields the initiative to Kejinan, with whom he acts in concert. But this is largely to avoid responsibility when trouble arises. He also harbors a dark cunning, ready to abandon Kejinan at any moment if the need arises. It was later revealed that his eyepatch was a mere decoration.',
        274: "Jaboli Mariera is a member of the Siberian Railway Guard. He is 23 years old. He was born and raised in the countryside and carries a strong inferiority complex about it. He admires Saint Reigan of London IMA, a city that represents urban sophistication, and especially Asuham, whom he adored as 'Lady White Lily.' Asuham called him the 'Wild Rose,' but in truth she seems to have thought of him as nothing more than a convenient pawn. He handles silhouette machines and Overmen competently, but he showed a side unaccustomed to violence, being poor with firearms since he had never shot a person. When he worked alongside the Kids, in contrast to Kejinan who was carried away by the promise of promotion, he lamented their low standing in the ranks - among the Siberian Railway troops, he was quite a man of conscience.",
        275: "Kashmar Barre is the operations chief of the Siberian Railroad. He is 39 years old. He detests any disruption to the railroad's timetable above all else, and his ruthlessness in maintaining the schedule by any means necessary has earned him the nickname 'the Ice Operations Chief.' He was dispatched as the captain of the railroad security force to fill the hole left by the vanished Yassaba, and above all to stop the Exodus of the 'Yapan Ceiling,' the very source of the timetable disruptions. He speaks in an effeminate manner, wears purple lipstick and a mohawk, and favors psycho Overmen that stoke anxiety or read minds - both in appearance and in substance, he is not a manly man. Aside from timetable disruptions, what he dislikes is healthy male-female relationships, and that once proved to be his undoing. In the end, he launched an attack with an Overman that projected terror, but because it touched Gain's inviolable domain, it ignited his anger, and he was blown to death as the black Southern Cross baptism struck his back.",
        276: "Asuham Boone is the captain of the Asuham Boone special forces unit of 'St. Reigan,' the police organization of the London IMA that administers Domepolis. His rank is special lieutenant. He is 28 years old. He is an elite with handsome looks and high practical ability, expected to have a bright future. His refined demeanor strongly attracted Jaboli. In truth, however, he has an impulsive and easily enraged personality, and he will calmly commit vile acts such as betrayal or taking hostages to achieve his goals. He is not merely a handsome face but, in a sense, a man full of humanity. He nominally cites stopping the Exodus as his reason, but above all he devotes himself to capturing Gain, repeatedly attacking the Yapan Ceiling. The reason is that Gain had previously made advances on Asuham's sister Karin and then left her, and Asuham sought to bring him back. Later, he deliberately left the elite course to corner Gain and transferred to the Siberian Railroad security force. He tried to use Cynthia and the Kids there, but his true goal was not achieved. Then, after the battle with the Overdevil, Karin, who had reunited with him, told him she had no intention of settling down with Gain, and he was dumbfounded to learn that all his efforts had been in vain.",
        277: "Zacky Bronco is the deputy captain of Asuham Boone's special forces unit in St. Reigan. He is 24 years old. He possesses ability befitting his position and handles Golem-type Overmen with ease. Though he follows Asuham's orders obediently, he privately holds a measure of contempt for Asuham, who pursues Gain with undisguised personal motives. When they made for the castle of Kids Munto, he was attacked and shot down by Cynthia's Dominator, sinking to the bottom of Lake Baikal. However, in the epilogue it was revealed that he had actually survived.",
        278: "Karin Boone is Asuham's beloved younger sister. Gain had previously made advances on her, and a child was conceived at that time. When she eventually gave birth to a girl, Asuham found himself fighting desperately to bring Gain back. After the conflict with the Overdevil was settled, she reunited with Asuham, and when he invited her to 'head to Gain's place together,' she declared that she had known from the start that Gain was not the kind of man to settle into a family, leaving Asuham stunned.",
        280: "Martina Lane is Cynthia's grandmother. She is a possessor of the powerful Over Sense inherited by her granddaughter. She has experienced Over Freeze firsthand and knows the terror of the Overdevil better than anyone. When Gainer wished to save Cynthia, who had been absorbed by the Overdevil, she taught him that he needed to unleash a true Over Sense exceeding 100 percent. Later, when Sara, who had been Over Frozen, took the Jinba and threatened the people of the 'Yapan Ceiling,' she rode the Panther and cut off both of its arms, showing off the height of her Over Sense.",
        281: "Cynthia Lane was the treasured child of the Kids Munto, and at 18 years of age she retained much of a childlike nature, always with sweets in her mouth, innocent in personality, and small of stature. However, her mother and grandmother came from a bloodline with powerful Over-Senses, and having been raised with elite training as an Overman pilot, she possessed combat ability beyond anything her appearance would suggest. She had long known Gainer as a rival and friend through games, holding the title of 'Queen,' the female counterpart to Gainer's title of 'King.' She tended to view combat in an Overman as an extension of gaming. As a result, she defeated the hesitant Gainer in real combat and wounded him, which sent her into strong shock and caused her to close her heart. Cynthia, who came to fear battle, was eventually absorbed by the Overdevil, dragging Gainer and Sara into the affair as well. Later, when Gainer, who had been the first to recover himself, activated his Over Heat, she was restored. She then gave a push to the backs of Gainer and Sara, who could not properly put their feelings into words.",
        282: "Eifa was a girl who ran a fortune-telling stall in Urgusk. She met the fugitive Yassaba and grew close to him when she gave him shelter. Having been mistreated by her master, she was invited by Yassaba to Exodus toward the Indus region, but she vanished into the blast from Golem fire meant to stop them. However, it appeared that Yassaba's arms had carried her through, and at the end she was confirmed to be continuing the Exodus energetically.",
        283: "Roger Smith was the preeminent negotiator of Paradigm City, a city that had lost its memories, aged 25. He carried out negotiations reliably with humorous and witty speech, delivering results beyond his clients' expectations. He was basically a feminist and a gentleman, but he was quick to anger, and toward those who would not listen to his words or who broke sincerity and rules, he would resort to force. However, it was his policy never to carry a gun, even on the most dangerous jobs. He had a past as a former military police lieutenant, and he knew Dastun from those days. He was a stubborn man who disliked bending his own views, but he also had an easygoing side, such as when Dorothy said she wanted a cat, and he ended up granting such earnest wishes despite his grumbling. He held the memory of piloting the Big O and faced great evils alongside it. This was never a pretense of being a champion of justice, but the result of straightforward anger toward those who broke sincerity or the rules of humanity. Roger himself did not know why he held the memory that allowed him to pilot the Big O. He made his home in a decayed bank on 72nd Street on the Out of Dome. Because Roger had an extreme preference for black, everyone living in his mansion was required to wear black clothes. Also, only women could enter his mansion unconditionally. His hobby was collecting hourglasses, and he also made them himself. While he placed great importance on a refreshing awakening, he had poor mornings, and scenes were seen of him being roused by Dorothy's extreme piano playing. After the battle with Big Fau, he negotiated with Big Venus, which appeared to reset the world, that is, with Angel, and succeeded brilliantly in the negotiation that determined the world's fate.",
        284: "R. Dorothy Wayneright was an android created by Timothy Wayneright in the likeness of his daughter, though her weight was quite heavy at 130 kilograms. Having no payment to offer for the affair concerning Wayneright's inheritance, she decided to work as a maid in Roger's mansion. She was made to be extremely human, not only highly complete as an android, but showing rich expressions to Wayneright, showing affection to cats, and posing questions about romance to Roger. As such, Roger was sometimes seen forgetting that she was an android. The 'R' stood for the 'R' in 'Robot.' Her sullen and high-handed attitude sometimes left Roger speechless, but as time passed she became a good partner to him. The hairband portion of her head was a memory drive and was often used as a light source as well. Piano playing was her hobby, but her initial repertoire consisted only of violent pieces. However, under the instruction of the pianist android R. Instol, the range of her performance gradually expanded. Alex extracted her memory drive and stopped her function, but she revived at Roger's moment of crisis and became the key to activating 'Big O Final Stage' as the Big O's interface.",
        285: "Norman Berg was the butler serving Roger, aged 54. Long before Roger came to the decayed bank, he had followed the memory of Big O maintenance and waited for his master to appear. He displayed a versatile ability for Roger every day, handling not only Big O maintenance but also the care of Roger's beloved car, the Griffon, and all household affairs of the mansion. It would be no exaggeration to say that Roger's private life was sustained thanks to him. He possessed an iron spirit unshaken by anything, and even when Roger was kidnapped, he worried but never lost composure, dealing with it calmly. He also showed a powerful side, racing through the battlefield on a large motorcycle with sidecar, and handling heavy firearms when enemies attacked. The repair of the Big O was not done by him alone, but by old men who, like him, held memories related to Big O maintenance.",
        286: 'Dan Dastun is the police chief of the Paradigm military police and commander of the mobile unit. He is 47 years old. He takes pride in his work with the military police and is a rugged man who faithfully follows his duties. He is also a man of justice who will defy orders from above and act on his own judgment to protect citizens, whether inside or outside the dome. Many subordinates admire him and act alongside him. His initial rank was major, but after being recognized for thwarting a foreign terrorist conspiracy, he was later promoted to colonel. He had a relationship with Roger, his former subordinate, marked by occasional conflict but mutual trust at heart, building a good friendship. During the Megadeus incident, he grew frustrated with his own powerlessness and that of the military police, and began to doubt the very worth of the military police as an institution. But after Roger was revealed as the pilot of Big O, he willingly took on the role of supporting him. In the final episode, to save Big O from a crisis, he showed his manly spirit by throwing away his military police badge, which was his pride, without hesitation.',
        287: "Angel is a mysterious woman whose nationality, age, and nearly everything else about her are shrouded in mystery. She calls herself Angel, perhaps because of scars on her back that look as though wings once grew there. Her motives are unclear, but she seems intent on obtaining memories, and she appears before Roger at every opportunity. She has a bold personality that does not flinch before anyone, and the drive to go even to the dangerous bottom of the sea if it means getting memories. She is employed by Paradigm Corporation, but her actions are not for the company's benefit; she simply seeks her own memories. In truth, she is an investigator belonging to the foreign organization Union, known by the code name Number 340. But in the final episode, it is revealed that her true identity is the memories themselves.",
        288: "Beck Jason is a criminal who commits misdeeds in Paradigm City. He is 22 years old. He appears with crude laughter and engages in all sorts of crimes, including bank robbery, kidnapping, and fraud. His words and actions are those of a small-time thug, and as Roger puts it, he is a 'criminal unworthy of the title professional.' Because he holds the memory of interface replacement technology crucial to piloting Megadeus, he procures Megadeus and uses them in his crimes. After being sent to prison by Roger in the Soldano heiress kidnapping case, he calls Roger 'Crow' and swears revenge. He repeatedly escapes from prison and devises schemes to bring Roger down, but all of them fail. Later, he is sentenced to death, but when the sentence is cancelled in exchange for forced cooperation with Paradigm Corporation, he reluctantly lends his hand. He finds it strange that Dorothy moves even after her memory unit is stolen, but in the end, he gives her advice on activating the 'Big O Final Stage' and watches the battle from afar.",
        291: "Schwarzwald is a memory digger who seeks the truth behind the memories lost over 40 years ago. He was once a newspaper reporter for Paradigm Press named Michael Seebach, but obsessed with pursuing the truth, he discovered the Archetype at the bottom of the underground corridors. However, when he unlocked it, his body became covered in bandages. Schwarzwald means 'black forest' in German. Later, he discovered Big Duo and challenged Roger to a duel, but was defeated. He was astonished when Big Duo moved on its own accord, and vanished from the public stage. He has a habit of speaking with meaningful phrases, as if reciting poetry. He looks down on those who do not seek the truth and merely live in the present. In truth, Angel revealed that Michael Seebach had died before the Big Duo incident.",
        292: "Alex Rosewater is the head of Paradigm Corporation, which rules Paradigm City. He is 43 years old. Born as the legitimate child of Gordon, who built the Paradigm Group, he boasts that he was chosen as the ruler, and is filled with a sense of omnipotence. Perhaps because of this, he has a childish side, and his self-centered words and actions stand out. He also holds strong elitist beliefs, thoroughly looking down on the residents who live outside the dome. He has a cold side, calmly eliminating targets for his goals, and had Alan collect fragments of memories. He thought Roger was the false dominus, but it was later revealed that he himself was the false dominus. Furthermore, when the fact that he was not even Gordon's legitimate child was thrust upon him, he went on a rampage in Big Fau, as if trying to have his existence acknowledged by others. But he was destroyed along with Big Fau by the sudden attack of Big Venus.",
        293: "A masked man who serves Alex and works behind the scenes. Because he is a 'Boogie' with half his body mechanized, he possesses remarkable physical abilities and regards himself as 'an existence that has transcended humanity.' He is cold-blooded and possesses an abnormal disposition that takes sadistic pleasure in killing. When he confronted Dorothy in a ruined church, he sent footage of a wounded Dorothy to the Big O's monitor, attempting to show Roger his atrocity. In truth, he was an agent of the Union, and he served as a bridge between the Union and Alex. However, in the end he betrayed the Union and sided with Alex. His code name was No. 271. When he boarded the Big Duo Inferno, perhaps because he became one with the machine through interface substitution technology, his personality became even more distorted and savage. In the end, the Big Duo Inferno judged him 'YE GULTY,' and he was swallowed up by the countless codes that welled forth.",
        294: "The first head of the Paradigm Group. At present, he has left the company to his heir Alex and devotes himself to cultivating artificial tomatoes at a farm on the outskirts of the city. His immense influence remains intact. He is a person who may know the truth of Memory, and when Roger visited him, he cast words suggesting that something had occurred between himself and Roger. Moreover, since a photograph of him in his youth shows him shaking hands with a man who looks exactly like Roger, there appears to be some kind of karmic connection between them. In his unfinished book 'Metropolis,' he recorded events that are thought to have occurred 40 years ago. After seeing off Angel in a dark space deep within Paradigm City, he expressed a wish that the true author of Metropolis should record Memory, and then vanished.",
        295: "A murderer clad in a red raincoat. He awoke from a container discarded beneath a marshaling yard and, using a handgun, killed one after another the people who had recalled memories from over 40 years ago. His motive was orders he heard from the moment of his awakening. The face beneath his hood was that of an android closely resembling Dorothy. The R stood for 'RED,' and the D for 'DESTINY.' When he aimed his gun at Roger to kill him as Roger investigated the case, he was caught between the fist of the Big O, which rose up from underground, and the ceiling, and was destroyed.",
        296: "A member of the foreign organization known as the Union, and its de facto leader. Her code name was No. 12. She appeared in Paradigm City to take responsibility for her subordinates' string of failures. Because she had led the Union members, she is thought to have held considerable power within the Union. However, after failing to punish Alex, who had betrayed the Union, and with many of her comrades captured, she rapidly lost her influence. In the final stages, she learned the true nature of Memory but, refusing to hand it to anyone else, activated an explosive device and vanished in the blast. At the same time, she awakened the land monster 'Behemoth' and had her own soul absorbed into it. The mother seen in Angel's memories was in fact herself.",
        297: 'An informant and acquaintance of Roger. Age 49. He is well versed in all manner of information, both within and outside Paradigm City. At the speak-easy bar, he always sits in the same seat, reading a newspaper while waiting for customers. In the final episode, beneath the skin of the man sitting in the ruined speak-easy could be seen the skeleton of an android.',
        298: "Pilot of the Gran Kaiser, and also serves as the main pilot during the Unite into God Gravion, Sol Gravion, and Ultimate Gravion. 17 years old. During his childhood in an orphanage, his strong G Factor was recognized, and he was adopted by Sandman. Since then, he has undergone repeated combat training at Saint-Germain Castle to become the Gran Kaiser's pilot. As a result, his personality has become quite detached from the everyday world. Normally gentle and personable, once on the battlefield he fells enemies with the coldness of a combat machine. In this state, he prioritizes destroying the enemy above all else and does not balk at some casualties. This imbalance sometimes wounds others without his being aware of it. When he revealed Leele's past, which everyone had tried to keep hidden, and shocked her, he showed a fragile side, disappearing in a daze. However, through his interactions with Eiji, his exact opposite, he came to recognize what he lacked and began to suffer. Finally, he realized that the warrior's path lies not in fighting to destroy the enemy, but in fighting to protect what is precious. Afterward, his emotions became richer, and when he learned that Eina, thought dead, was alive, he wept tears of joy.",
        299: "Pilot of the G Attacker, which forms the right leg of God Gravion, and of the Geo Mirage, which forms the chest and head of Sol Gravion. 17 years old. His surname is read 'Shigure.' Since childhood, his older sister Ayaka, who raised him, has been the most important person to him, making him a fierce sister-complex. When she went missing, he infiltrated Saint-Germain Castle alone to search for her. By chance, he boarded the G Attacker, and that became the catalyst for his becoming a pilot. His personality is hot-blooded, and he is a troublemaker for whom ignoring orders and going out without permission are everyday occurrences. To Touga, he is a true bad friend, filling the naive Touga with various knowledge and dragging him into reckless situations. Meanwhile, Eiji, burning with rivalry toward Touga, once boarded the Gran Kaiser himself. However, he clashed with Touga many times over his willingness to sacrifice others in battle and his attitude of not considering people's feelings. Even so, they recognized each other and gradually built a good relationship. During the final battle against Zeravire, he was shocked to learn that Raven was Ayaka. She apologized for hiding her identity, but he forgave her without a single complaint.",
        300: "Pilot of the G Driller, which forms the left arm of God Gravion, and of the Geo Javelin, which forms the left arm of Sol Gravion. 16 years old. Her surname is read 'Gusuku.' A lively girl from Okinawa. Her emotions show directly, so her expressions are quite rich. She possesses the bravery to face even harsh battles without fear. Since meeting Touga at Saint-Germain Castle, where her father brought her as a child, she has harbored a faint love for him. For that reason, she is jealous of Eiji, who, despite being another boy, appeared later and grew close to Touga. This seems to be one reason the two of them never stop quarreling. She deeply respects her late father, and she joined the Grand Knights to carry on his will, as he had risked his life to report the discovery of Zeravire. During the final battle, Ayaka, having removed Raven's mask, told her that her father had been the previous Raven. Learning anew of her father's greatness, her heart was filled with warmth.",
        301: 'Pilot of the G Striker, which forms the left leg of God Gravion, and of the Geo Stinger, which forms the left leg of Sol Gravion. 22 years old. A combat professional trained at Saint-Germain Castle. She provides spiritual support to the Grand Knights, whose members are often immature. She has a hobby of seducing men, and during a hot spring trip she reverse-picked-up Alex. Yet she has the difficult personality of having no interest in men who fall for her. She is close friends with Ayaka and cooperated with Eiji in his search for her, who was thought to be somewhere in Saint-Germain Castle. However, her true identity was that of a spy infiltrated by the EFA to investigate Sandman and Gravion. The Gravion data she gathered was fed back into the development of the Gran Trooper. With the Gran Trooper completed, her role ended, and she left the Grand Knights to rejoin the military. Yet unable to sever her bonds with the Grand Knights, she decided to return to Asgard. Together with her comrades, bound by ties stronger than ever, she faced the final battle against Zeravire.',
        302: "Pilot of the G Driller, which forms the right arm of God Gravion. Her apparent age is 16. Usually she works as a maid at Saint-Germain Castle. She is serious and hardworking in everything, always striving to be useful to someone, but her innate clumsiness often ends up causing trouble for those around her. Even so, since she looked after Touga from his childhood, she is like a mother to him. She is timid and lacks confidence in herself, but she harbors a strong will to risk her life for her comrades without hesitation. This became clear when Touga was captured by Zeravire and she, without a moment's hesitation, charged the enemy to save him, giving her own life to rescue him. And she had a great secret. In truth, she was a copy of the artificial lifeform 'Proto Grandiva' created by Sandman, which was why she had maintained the same appearance for decades. Upon her death, the original, sleeping on the moon, awakened and later returned, bringing Sol Gravion with it.",
        304: 'Leele is the pilot of the G Shadow, which forms the head and chest of God Gravion, and the Geo Caliver, which forms the right leg of Sol Gravion. She is 14 years old. She spends all her time, except when on sortie, with her pet and best friend, a ferret named Lolo. She was found collapsed and having lost her memory, and was taken in by Sandman. Since then, she lived in the south tower of Saint-Germain Castle without contact with any humans other than Sandman. As a result, she initially kept her heart closed to others, but as she continued to fight and live daily life as a member of the Grand Knights, a sense of camaraderie blossomed, and she gradually began to show a variety of expressions. Later, it was revealed that Sandman was her biological father, and that the enemy leader was her uncle. Though deeply shocked by the reality thrust upon her, she showed an inner strength to overcome and accept it with the help of her comrades.',
        305: 'Sandman is the lord of Saint-Germain Castle and a world-class tycoon. With his knowledge and wealth, he organized Asgard and, as its supreme commander, protects the peace of Earth. However, his past and background remain shrouded in mystery. He is a man of unique aesthetics, flawless in everything he does, always carrying it out in style. He has many fans even among the maids working at Saint-Germain Castle. Yet, because he carries the shameful secret of his past alone, he has shown a human side, quietly retreating into his own shell at times.',
        306: "Klain Sandman is an assumed name; his real name is 'Zig Erickmeier'. He is a scientist from the planet Lambias, who developed the Genesis Machine 'Gran Sigma', capable of destroying or even creating planets, in order to save his doomed homeworld. However, a difference of opinion led to a clash with his brother-in-law Hughie, and as a result Lambias collapsed. He escaped Lambias in the 'Gran Sigma' and eventually reached Earth. Then, to protect Earth from his brother-in-law, who he knew would one day come seeking revenge, he spent many long years building the Proto Grandiva and God Gravion, among others. By using the G Factor within his body as a metabolic function, his hair color changed to purple and he gained immortality. However, because he boarded the 'Gran Sigma' and released the G Factor in order to fight, his hair has returned to its original blonde. After the battle with Zeravire ended, he was united with Ayaka, who had saved him both physically and mentally.",
        307: "Raven is the combat commander of Asgard. He always hides his face behind a mask, which cannot be removed without Sandman's permission. He possesses a strong will, always maintaining the composure to correctly assess situations. When an emergency occurs, he gives precise orders to the Grand Knights and the combat maid unit. He enjoys Sandman's deep trust and becomes the highest authority in his absence. Because of this position, he is often left behind as caretaker when others go on vacations or to hot springs, much to his deep lament. Training the Grand Knights is also his duty, and he is especially hard on Eiji. During Zeravire's full-scale invasion, he removed his mask to rouse Sandman, who was cowering in fear of Hughie's shadow, with his own voice and words. His true identity is Eiji's sister, Ayaka. 'Raven' was the name of a young man who served as Sandman's assistant on the planet Lambias, and since then, it has been customary for those who assist Sandman to inherit that name. Before Ayaka, Runa's father held the mask. The mask stores the memories of all previous Ravens, and inheriting them allows one to draw out the necessary abilities. In addition, it is a product of terrifying technology that can change not only one's body shape but even their gender.",
        308: "Ayaka is Eiji's older sister. A former member of the EFA, she fell in love with Sandman while spying on Saint-Germain Castle. Though she possessed the G Factor, its power was too weak for her to pilot the Grandiva. To support him instead, she chose the path of inheriting the 'Raven' title, hiding her identity without even telling her close friend Mizuki the truth. When she faced the Grand Knights for training or punishment as 'Raven', she was especially strict with Eiji. Whether this was out of sisterly affection or as punishment for his rude remarks to Sandman remains a fine line. When Sandman lost his will to fight, cowering in fear of Hughie's shadow, she removed the Raven mask and roused him with her own words. During the final battle with Zeravire, she moved the heart of Sandman, who was prepared to share his fate with the collapsing Goma, and saved his life. Her efforts were rewarded, as she was later duly united with Sandman.",
        317: "Faye Shinluu is the captain of the G Soldier squad belonging to Earth Federation Government EFA, with the rank of Lieutenant. Written in kanji, her name is ''. During combat with Gran Troopers, she gives formation orders to each unit. She possesses excellent piloting skills, outstanding athletic ability, and a sharp intellect, and is trusted deeply by both subordinates and superiors.\nShe spent her early childhood in the same orphanage as Touga, but the fact that Sandman took in Touga instead of her became a complex, and she resolved to always be more capable than Touga. That feeling became a burden, and there were times in battle when she misjudged the moment to withdraw. She often scolded her subordinate Alex for his unserious attitude, but their relationship was by no means a bad one. When she lost sight of her reason for being before the final battle with Zeravire, his encouragement cut through her hesitation, and she sortied to support the Gran Knights.\nIn the final battle, she was saved from a desperate crisis by Sandman, and it was there that she was finally able to cast aside her fixation on the past.",
        318: "Alex Smith is a member of the G Soldier squad belonging to Earth Federation Government EFA, with the rank of Lieutenant. He was originally in the air force, serving as a fighter pilot. However, he was wounded in an attack by Zeravire during a mission, and after recovering, he was transferred into the G Soldier squad. From then on, he came to pilot a Gran Trooper whose main armament was a gun.\nHe is basically a light-hearted person, and his likes are girls, robots, and Japan. Faye repeatedly admonished him for his exuberant remarks, but even during the final battle, he spoke lines he 'had always wanted to say', and asked for a handshake from Sandman's God Sigma Gravion, never breaking his fundamental style to the very end. He also encouraged a troubled Faye and, even in desperate danger, endured while believing in the arrival of Gravion, showing a passionate side that proves he was no mere joker.",
        322: 'William Wallace Fitzgerald is the supreme commander of the Earth Federation Government EFA, holding the office of President. He was capable and frank in personality, and handled government affairs without issue, but was hard-pressed by the sudden appearance of Zeravire. Then, too fixated on his pride as supreme leader, he took an uncooperative attitude toward Sandman, who possessed the power of Gravion.\nIn order to repel Zeravire with EFA alone, he had Gran Troopers developed, using data that Mizuki had gathered as a reference. However, once it became clear that nothing but Gravion could oppose Zeravire, he came to cooperate fully with Sandman.',
        323: "Hugi Zeravire is the older brother of Sandman's wife Lufira, and the one who leads the Zeravire. He was originally an excellent scientist, and in order to save the residents of his home planet Lambias, which was perishing due to environmental degradation, he developed the slaughter system 'Genocidron' to annihilate the people of Planet Caelias and secure a place for immigrants. However, he clashed with Sandman, who advocated environmental restoration through the Genesis Star 'Gran Sigma', and in an accident during that clash, he was seized by a runaway 'Genocidron'.\nAfter being absorbed into the system, his thirst for revenge against Sandman was amplified, and he lost his mental balance. Believing that Sandman was responsible for the death of his beloved sister Lufira, he came to resolve to attack Earth with the destruction machine 'Zeravire' that the system created.\nYet even while imprisoned by the 'Genocidron', he did not completely lose his humanity, keeping an artificial life-form modeled after Lufira at his side and incorporating a program to protect his niece Leele into the 'Zeravire'. During the final battle with Sandman, that became his undoing. And just before his death, he was finally freed from the system's curse.",
        324: "Lufira is Hugi's younger sister. She was united with Sandman, and bore him a beloved daughter, Leele. Originally frail of health, she could not withstand the burden of childbirth and passed away in exchange for Leele's birth. However, she was revived as an artificial life-form by Hugi, who could not accept her death.\nNo soul dwelt within her, and she became a puppet obedient to Hugi's commands. But when she witnessed Sandman being wounded in the battle against Hugi, she worked the miracle of housing a soul within her body. In the end, she was consumed by flames inside the collapsing Goma, together with her brother's remains.",
        326: "Apollo is a boy believed to be the reincarnation of Apollonius, the 'Wing of the Sun.' His estimated age is 13. After becoming an orphan during the great catastrophe 11 years ago, he joined forces with Baron and others in the same situation and lived vigorously as a street child. In addition to his rare wild instincts, he possesses phenomenal eyesight of 5.0 or better in both eyes, and an excellent sense of smell that can distinguish not only body odor but even the scent of infrared rays, making him worthy of being called a wild child. His personality is straightforward for better or worse, and he tends to act in ways that could be taken as selfish. Though he seems to lack any sense of solidarity, he harbors a passionate friendship that fears no danger for the sake of his comrades. He boarded Aquarion in order to rescue Baron, who had been captured by the Shadow Angels. For a while after entering Element School, he caused frequent trouble due to his unfamiliarity with group life and stand play. However, through battles he acquired cooperation and teamwork, and along with that, he began to remember his past life. When the crisis of the world's end arrived after the final battle, he overcame past frictions and conflicts to complete the Genesis union with Sirius and Zushi (Toma), becoming a pillar to save the world. At that time, he appeared before Silvia as a spiritual body, offering a farewell kiss and a promise to meet again 12,000 years later.",
        327: "Silvia is a first-class Element attending Element School. She is 14 years old. She is a princess of the old Kingdom of Alisia, carrying the bloodline of Apollonius and Celian. She possesses the ability to emit psychokinetic force by gathering ki in her left arm, allowing her to lift or bend any object. Perhaps because she lost her parents at a young age, she harbors an abnormal affection for her older brother Sirius. As a result, she is wary of all women who approach Sirius, and particularly holds hostility toward Reika. She carries the past life of Celian and was convinced that the reincarnation of her former lover, the 'Wing of the Sun,' was Sirius. However, when faced with the fact that Apollo, a wild child who suddenly appeared one day, might actually be the 'Wing of the Sun,' she stubbornly refused to accept it. But aided by her own memories of her past life, she gradually came to acknowledge it. Along with Sirius, she bears a Shadow Angel wing deeply connected to her past life on her left arm, hidden beneath her wristband. After Sirius defected to the Shadow Angels' side, she too received an invitation from her brother. However, upon hearing Apollo's words, she decided to live as a human and refused Sirius's invitation. When the end of the world arrived after the final battle, she made Apollo and Sirius, who continued to fight, and Zushi (Toma) aware of the existence of light born from darkness through the memories of Celian. Though she was ultimately separated from Apollo, with whom she had connected emotionally in both her past life and the present, she was certain that he would someday return to this planet.",
        328: "Sirius is a first-class Element attending Element School. He is 16 years old. He is a prince of the old Kingdom of Alisia and Silvia's older brother. He cherishes a rose he named Alicia, recites poetry at every opportunity, and pours his affection on all things beautiful. He acknowledges Reika's bearing as beautiful and holds feelings for her. However, because he thoroughly rejects things that are ugly and barbaric, the opposite of beauty, he constantly clashes with Apollo, who is a mass of wildness. Regarding Apollo, however, his frustration at being unable to recall his own past life and jealousy toward him are also greatly involved. He possesses an Element ability that emits high-frequency vibrations from his right arm, and by transmitting this to a sword, he can produce astonishing cutting power. His hearing also far exceeds that of ordinary people. Along with his younger sister Silvia, he bears a Heavenly Wing deeply connected to his past life on his right arm, hidden beneath his wristband. Later, when Zushi invited him to Atlandia, Reika, who reached out to stop him, saw the wing and instinctively pulled her hand back. Shocked by that reaction, Sirius realized there was no longer a place for him on the earth and fell to the Heavenly Wings.",
        329: "Reika is a first-class Element attending Element School. She is 15 years old. Her name is read 'Kou-Reika.' Her Element abilities are strong spiritual sensitivity and psychometry that reads records. However, because these abilities are too powerful, she attracts trouble wherever she goes. She is a self-acknowledged 'woman who invites misfortune.' Fearing that she will involve those who approach her, she tends to show an atmosphere that keeps others at a distance and a dark, gloomy expression. But in truth, she has a rich sensibility, and her skills include sports in general, making her active. When Glen was seriously wounded on her first sortie, she believed it was due to the misfortune she spreads and feared combining, sinking even deeper into gloom. However, through Commander Fudo's training and surviving battles, she gradually overcame her negative emotions. When Glen was revived after receiving a transplanted Shadow Angel wing, she was bewildered by his emotionless continued fighting. Unable to leave him in danger, she went to his rescue, and that became the catalyst for Glen to successfully regain his sense of self. Glen later lost his life in battle, but the grown Reika continued fighting without stopping and succeeded in cutting off her own misfortune.",
        330: 'Pierre is a first-class Element attending Element School. He is 17 years old. He possesses the Element ability to control fire, a hot-blooded man burning in both body and spirit. He was once active as a professional soccer player, but joined DEAVA after his team members and all the spectators were taken by a Mythical Beast during a match. Considering himself the mood maker of the Elements, he always brightens the atmosphere with his inherent cheerfulness. However, when Apollo ran wild thinking only of himself, he showed a sportsmanlike side that values harmony, shouting at him to cooperate and face the enemy. Though he is thought to be a frivolous man who hits on any woman he sees, this actually stems from his own bravado to cover up the heartbreak of his first love, Esperansa, having married his older brother Lopez. Before sortieing with the final battle approaching, his usual lightness paid off (?) as Chloe confessed her feelings to him, and he accepted them.',
        331: "Jun is a first-class Element attending the Element School. He is 14 years old. He is skilled with machines and computers, and truly shines in mental work such as information analysis. His knowledge of hacking is especially deep, and he can access state secrets at will. On the other hand, his lack of physical fitness is notable, and he always struggles with the training imposed by Commander Fudo. He is also an idol otaku, and a favorite figure, 'Manamana-chan', is displayed on the PC in his room. As an Element, he possesses the ability of thoughtography, projecting images onto film or digital screens. However, he cannot see the image directly until it is actually projected. He holds feelings for Tsugumi, who entered the Element School at the same time, but her heart seems to be elsewhere, and their relationship never progresses. Before the final battle, he resolved himself and gave her a present, but...",
        332: 'Tsugumi is a first-class Element attending the Element School. She is 15 years old. She is a bright and cheerful girl, but she sometimes makes major blunders. Though her usual timid demeanor makes it hard to imagine, she also hides a passionate side that goes straight for what she believes in. She also seems to harbor feelings of admiration, more than mere respect, for her senior Reika. Her hobby and specialty is tinkering with machines, and her skill is such that she once repaired her beloved car, the Isetta, which she received from her grandfather. Her Element ability causes explosions around her when her excitement reaches its peak. Because of this, she was shunned by others in childhood, and it remains a trauma even now. Even when she first entered the school, she kept her ability hidden and refused sortie orders, but after being persuaded by Jun, she decided to sortie. She defeated the enemy splendidly and overcame her trauma. When heading to the final battle, she piloted Aquarion Angel and, using her explosion ability, broke through the gate to Atlandia.',
        333: "Reena is an Element belonging to DEAVA, a mysterious girl of unknown age. She possesses very strong psychic sensitivity and has the Element ability to judge people's hearts and the surrounding environment through the shape and color of auras. She is also a prophet who performs various divinations using the 'Book of Genesis', and her ability is highly valued within DEAVA. She absorbs prana from blood and can teleport without using the Element Change System, and due to her many mysteries, even suspicions of her being a vampire once circulated. But with Apollo's help, her comrades eventually came to recognize her, including her special powers, as simply being Reena. She boarded a Vector Machine only twice, during the vampire incident and the final battle, which is very few times. But on both sorties, she aided her comrades with excellent ability and judgment.",
        334: 'Glen was a first-class Element who achieved results at the Element School on par with Sirius and Reika. He was 17 years old. He had a kind personality and also possessed excellent qualities as an Element. He had built a solid relationship of trust with Sirius and the others. In his first real battle, he united with Reika, whom he had feelings for. However, during that battle he was hit and severely wounded. Afterward, he remained in a coma, and his recovery was thought to be hopeless. But later, he had the wings of a Shadow Angel transplanted into him, and appeared with the Assault-Type Aquarion while his consciousness remained sealed.',
        335: "Glen, revived from his coma after having the wings of Zushi transplanted into him. He has lost the kindness he once showed, and has become an expressionless, cold-hearted combat machine. He stood in the way of the Cherudim Mars piloted by Shishi, who was attempting to break DEAVA's barrier, using the Assault-Type Aquarion. During the final battle, his consciousness gradually revived upon hearing Reika's cry as she was attacked by Ryoshi, and the feelings for her sleeping in the depths of his memory brought him back to himself. He then stopped Reika, who said she would fight alongside him, made her go on ahead, and defeated Ryoshi at the cost of his life. At the end, his soul went to Reika, and he vanished, leaving a smile behind.",
        336: 'Chloe Kurik is a first-class Element attending the Element School. She is 14 years old. Apart from their clothing, she has virtually no physical differences from her fraternal twin brother Kurt. She possesses the Element ability of telepathy, which manifests most powerfully between her and Kurt. She sometimes sortied riding a Vector Machine, but as her support abilities were apparently stronger, she primarily took part in combat as an operator. Though she does not show it outwardly, she frets over the fact that her overly serious nature leaves her ignored by the opposite sex. She harbors feelings for Pierre, the only one who ever spoke to her, and confesses these feelings just before the final battle.',
        337: 'Kurt Kurik is a first-class Element attending the Element School. He is 14 years old. Apart from their clothing, he has virtually no physical differences from his fraternal twin sister Chloe. He possesses the Element ability of telepathy, which manifests most powerfully between him and Chloe. He sometimes sortied riding a Vector Machine, but as his support abilities were apparently stronger, he primarily took part in combat as an operator. Just before the final battle, he learns that Chloe has feelings for Pierre, and is shocked by this revelation.',
        338: "Fudo GEN is the commander of the Aquarion deployment unit of the special agency 'Earth Restoration Organization DEAVA.' He also holds the position of instructor at the Element School. His age is unknown. He is known as the 'Magician of Divine Speed' for his ability to appear and disappear at will, showing up anywhere. He has mastered a wide and deep range of skills, from magic-like tricks such as producing arrows from nowhere or suddenly enlarging sheets of paper, to astonishing abilities like reading people's minds, calling wild hawks with a single finger, and discerning a person's personality and preferences merely from their footprints. Aside from having been a member of the Aquarion excavation survey team, his past history is entirely unknown. Even how he became commander is unclear, making him a man of many mysteries, but his words carry a strange persuasiveness. He constantly gives the Elements hints for overcoming difficulties, leading them to victory. As for his true nature, there are rumors that in the Atlandia War 12,000 years ago, he was an 'Element whose existence was sealed away' who piloted Aquarion alongside Apollonius and Celiane, but the truth remains unknown.",
        339: "Jean Jerome Georges is the vice commander of DEAVA's Aquarion deployment unit. He is 24 years old. Since he was still a boy, he has been involved in the organization's founding, and several members of his family hold positions in DEAVA's upper echelons. He holds various doctorates in military and defense studies, and possesses a genius intellect having mastered thirteen languages. However, his overly serious personality works against him, as he cannot bend the rules and can only conduct operations lacking flexibility, which is his weakness. As a result, before Commander Fudo, who leads the Elements with bold actions and weighty words, he tended to fade into the background. Additionally, the reckless and undisciplined behavior of the overly individualistic Elements is a constant source of headaches for him. In the final battle against the Shadow Angels, he opposes the new United Nations military's plan to prioritize the annihilation of Atlandia even at the cost of abandoning captured people, and declares that DEAVA will act on its own. Before he knew it, he too had come under Fudo GEN's influence, and the sight of him issuing sortie orders to Aquarion was the very image of the commander he had aspired to be.",
        341: "Baron is Apollo's best friend and the leader figure among the street children. When Baron first met Apollo, the latter had no name, but Baron, who appeared as if emerging from the rising morning sun, bestowed upon him the name 'Apollo.' Before Apollo's very eyes, he was carried off by a Harvest Beast along with the other companions. Later, by the machinations of Zushi <Toma>, he is brought before Apollo while imprisoned. Apollo attempts to pry open the cage restraining him with Aquarion, but a bomb rigged to the cage explodes before his eyes, and they are parted forever.",
        342: "Head Wing <Toma> is a holy wing of the Shadow Angels, serving as the frontline commander who leads the other wings. He bears a wing on the back of his head, but apart from that, he has the most human-like appearance among the Shadow Angels. Twelve thousand years ago, he was betrothed to Apollonius, the strongest guardian wing. However, when Apollonius betrayed the Shadow Angels near the end of the Atlandia War, they crossed blades as enemies. Yet his love has not faded even now, and he repeatedly makes contact with Apollo, who appears to be Apollonius's reincarnation. In the course of battle, he killed Apollo's close friend Baron, and used honeyed words to seduce Sirius into defecting, using various means to torment Apollo and his allies. But when the Tree of Life withered and the world faced a crisis of annihilation, he went so far as to teleport to Vector Luna in an attempt to stop it. Even so, he could not see eye to eye with Apollo and Sirius, but through the memories of Celian that Silvia revealed, he learned that Apollonius had not betrayed them long ago, but had wished for coexistence between wings and humans. Once he resolved to carry on that will, the three of them succeeded in the Genesis Unite and held together the shattering world. Incidentally, 'Shadow Angel' is a derogatory term used by humans for the wings, and they call themselves 'Wings' (the human derogatory term on the Shadow Angel side is 'wingless' or 'wingless people'). However, it may be that only Apollonius, who betrayed the Shadow Angels, can truly be called a 'Shadow Angel' in their eyes.",
        343: "Sound Wing <Otoha> is the music wing of the Shadow Angels. At a glance she appears to be a beautiful woman, but beneath her robes she conceals a serpent-like lower body. Also, what appear to be her eyebrows are actually eyes, and when her emotions run high, all four eyes open wide. She is the lover of the holy wing Head Wing <Toma> in the present age, and she burns with dark flames of jealousy toward Apollonius, who still captivates his heart. The wings covering both her arms can be strummed like a harp or made to produce delicate vibrations to play music. Though the tones are beautiful, they harbor powerful enchantment that can drive listeners mad or even manipulate the weather. In the final battle at Atlandia, she relentlessly attacked Aquarion Alpha, but her body was cut down along with Reika's misfortune.",
        345: "Both Wing <Moroha> is a war wing of the Shadow Angels. He is a combat-type Shadow Angel with a visage blending human and insect, featuring a pair of sword-like arms in addition to his normal ones, and insect-like wings on his back. The eyes peering from the cloth covering his face convey no emotion, giving him a strongly aggressive and intimidating presence. Being belligerent and self-confident, he holds a fierce rivalry with Head Wing <Toma> and constantly takes a challenging attitude, but he possesses the ability to back it up. He commands his own Cherudim soldier 'Cherudim Ischyrion' and overwhelmed the Aquarion throughout. However, he was brought down in a mutual strike by Glen, who had been freed from the curse of the wings.",
        348: "Twin Wing <Futaba> is the last small wing remaining among the Shadow Angels. She bears wings on her ankles, and parts of her body, such as her shoulders and arms, have machinery attached. After the Atlandia War twelve thousand years ago, children had almost stopped being born among the Shadow Angels, making her a precious existence who was doted on by the other wings. Perhaps because of this, she grew into a very spoiled and mischievous child. Driven by her abundant curiosity, she constantly comes up with pranks (which are nightmares of calamity for humans) and carries them out. She takes a liking to Apollonius's wing, which brings destruction upon beautiful sounds, and ignoring the warnings of Wisdom Wing <Shiruha>, she goes out alone to attack the city. However, she is captured by DEAVA's secretly completed capture system 'Kagome Operation'. Then her wings are taken for study of her body, and she loses her life. The Shadow Angels deeply mourn her death and resolve to take revenge on humanity.",
        350: "Poem Wing <Sirius> is Sirius, who defected to the Shadow Angels. Believing without doubt that he himself was the Wing of the Sun, he fought fierce battles against the Aquarion in Cherudim Mars, a fusion of Vector Mars and a Cherudim soldier. However, the truth he eventually heard from Head Wing <Toma>'s mouth was that Poem Wing <Sirius> was the reincarnation of Celian, and moreover carried the dark memories. As he reeled in shock at this fact, Cherudim Mars moved against his will and fired a spear of light at Silvia. But Poem Wing <Sirius>, regaining control, shielded his sister by taking the spear on Cherudim Mars. After the final battle, guided by Silvia, he completed the Genesis Unite of Apollo and Head Wing <Toma> to save the imperiled world and revived the earth.",
        351: "The strongest guardian of the Shadow Angels. Twelve thousand years ago, he used his great power to hunt and slaughter countless humans. But during battle, he met the human warrior woman Cerian, and the two fell in love with each other. Eventually he parted ways with the Shadow Angels and began to fight alongside humanity, using the 'Mechanical Angel Aquarion' to sink Atlandia into subspace. In the final battle, it was revealed through Cerian's past life that his decision to side with humanity during the Great Atlandia War had been to seek a world where humans and Shadow Angels could coexist. His resolve moved Apollo, Sirius, and Zushi (Toma), and led them to decide to become the pillars that would save the world.",
        352: "A brave human warrior woman who fought the Shadow Angels twelve thousand years ago. She met Apollonius during battle, and despite being enemies, they fell in love. Later they joined forces and defeated the Shadow Angels with the 'Mechanical Angel Aquarion'. In the present day, Silvia carries the beautiful memories of light from Cerian's past lives, so her personality occasionally surfaces. The terrible memories of darkness, meanwhile, were inherited by Sirius.",
        353: "A boy whose father was a hero who once saved the world. Fourteen years old. He is simple and pure-hearted, bright and optimistic - a personality that is too straightforward. Because of this, when he gets too absorbed in something, he loses sight of everything around him. Also, since everything he thinks shows on his face, the adults around him often tease him for it. He is also at the age where being seen through the lens of 'the hero's son' irritates him. He lives with his grandfather in the rural town of Bellforest, and while dissatisfied with his boring, unchanging daily life, he idly spends his days working on his bike and lift board. However, when he fell in love at first sight with Eureka, who suddenly descended from the sky, he joined Gekkostate at the invitation of his idol Holland and Eureka herself. While being worked hard as an errand boy, he also rides in the Nirvash alongside Eureka during sorties. At first he only sat in the sub-seat, but gradually he began to show promise as a rider. In time he became indispensable to Gekkostate, and to Eureka. But when an incident saw Eureka, after falling ill, get absorbed into the Scub Coral, the situation began to change. Gekkostate was not merely a lift board gang; the fact that he had killed people in battle; and Eureka, who did not understand him. Unable to bear a reality so different from his ideals, he once left the Gekko-Goh. Even so, through experiences such as meeting and parting with people who might have become his parents, making up with Eureka, and the plunge into the Zone, he grew greatly as a person.",
        355: "An LFO rider belonging to Gekkostate who pilots the Nirvash. A girl with mysterious abilities - she can hear the voices of LFOs and machines to communicate with them, and can read the otherwise invisible flow of trapar. Not only are her words and actions far removed from common sense, she shows little emotion and very rarely smiles. But as if dragged along by Renton's brightness, she gradually opened her heart. She acts as a surrogate mother to three orphaned children, and when she was first called 'Mama', Renton was astonished. In truth, she has a past of belonging to a special forces unit in the Federation Army, where she killed the citizens of the city Ciudad del Cielo on orders. The children are survivors of that massacre.",
        356: "Eureka after being absorbed into the Scub Coral and rescued. The truth is that she is a humanoid Coralian, and according to the high monk of Vodarac, she was in a state called the 'Seventh Observation World' (humans exist in the Third Observation World). After waking, she realized the feelings for Renton that had sprouted within her, and showed decisiveness and initiative by setting out alone to search for Renton, who had run away from home.",
        357: 'After meeting Sakuya and crossing the Zone together with Renton and the children, this is Eureka as she appears afterward.\nIt seems she has returned to the Third Observation World, and her hair and blood vessels have reverted to their state before they were absorbed into the Scub Coral. However, her changes did not stop there.',
        358: "As if triggered by the breakthrough of the Zone, Eureka underwent changes in her body.\nHer left arm became a translucent green, and similar patches appeared elsewhere on her body. On her back, organs resembling a combination of butterfly wings and the fins of marine creatures grew out.\nAt first, she could not hide her confusion at her own transformation. The children felt the same way. But even so, Renton's actions in accepting Eureka brought everyone's hearts together, and the five became a true family.",
        359: "The leader of the anti-establishment group Gekkostate. Age 29.\nHe possesses lift techniques that earned him the title of youngest champion at the amateur lift world tournament, and he is a charismatic figure among lift boarders. Renton also had a strong admiration for him, putting up posters of him in his room and using a replica lift board.\nHe is an excessive self-confident and always leads the members with a strong attitude. Even so, the fact that he never loses his composure while lifting is what makes him who he is.\nHe once belonged to the Federation of the Tower State's military, but defected after a certain incident. He seized the Gekko-Goh and the Nirvash and organized Gekkostate. He is romantically involved with Talho, but since all his actions prioritize Eureka above all, this has become a source of trouble.\nWith Renton, who somewhat resembles his former self, minor conflicts seem to never cease. But having accepted the fact that he was not chosen by Eureka, and perhaps aided by his awareness of becoming a father, he eventually deepened his trust in Renton to the point of entrusting Eureka to him.\nHis real name is Holland Novak, and he had long been in conflict with his older brother Dewey. After settling that grudge, his face as he saw off Renton, who took flight to save Eureka, was the most cheerful it had ever been.",
        362: "A cameraman accompanying Gekkostate. Age 30.\nHe fights using a pen stronger than the sword, handling the writing and editorial work for the magazine 'ray=out' published to spread Gekkostate's activities to the world.\nWhen battle begins, he mostly rides in the rear seat of the R606 and devotes himself to taking photographs on the battlefield. At such times, he gives Matthew detailed instructions on altitude and speed, and as his words 'Art is something you risk your life for' suggest, he shows a nerve that is steadier than any rider's.\nAs he consistently devoted his passion to pursuing the truth, he gradually approached the core of the world through conversations with Doctor Bear and Norbu. However, his grumbling at having failed to photograph Renton's heroic figure when he made his final sortie in the Nirvash spec3 was purely that of just another cameraman.",
        366: "The gunnery officer of the Gekko-Goh. Age 45.\nAs evident from his appearance and demeanor, he was a strict, no-nonsense soldier, but his meeting with Holland greatly shook his view of life, and he subsequently came to act alongside the Gekko-Goh.\nHe is the oldest among the official Gekkostate members, and with a presence that could be called that of a master and deep combat experience, he is a dependable man.\nIn handling firearms, he shows considerable skill, hitting enemy ships with laser cannons from outside their range and performing emergency evasive maneuvers using the recoil of the main cannon.\nWhen Moondoggie took over piloting duties in place of Talho, he spurred on and encouraged the boy, who was bewildered by unfamiliar real combat, and brought out his talent to the fullest. Seeing this, Hap praised them as 'a good pair.'",
        367: "Moondoggie is a member of Gekkostate. He is 16 years old. Although he has a beautiful appearance, when he opens his mouth he speaks with a strong dialect. Because he himself is conscious of this gap, he speaks little. He was the comic relief among the members, but when the newcomer Renton threatened his position, he briefly felt a sense of rivalry. However, after various twists and turns, he came to be called 'Doggie aniki' by Renton and was looked up to. Perhaps due to a certain kindred spirit, they seem to get along quite well. He is inwardly concerned about having no role during combat, and scenes were seen where he took out his frustration on his partner Gidget and the children. But when Talho was away on an infiltration mission, he voluntarily took on the role of helmsman. Whether his skill was recognized or not, from then on the fate of the Gekko-Goh was entrusted to his shoulders. When he presented his boating license, it was revealed that his real name is 'James Darren Emerson'.",
        368: "Gidget is the communications officer of the Gekko-Goh. She is 15 years old. She is somewhat obsessively clean and has a fangirl side, but alongside the small and cheerful Eureka, she is one of the idols of the Gekko-Goh. She harbors feelings for Moondoggie and is always clinging to him and fussing over him outside of combat. Toward Eureka, who is close in age, she tries to build a friendship like the one between Talho and Hilda, and offers advice whenever something comes up. Her greatest achievement was probably teaching Eureka that the feelings she holds for Renton are 'love'.",
        371: "Mischa is the resident doctor of the Gekko-Goh. She is 40 years old. She was devoted to the study of Eureka even when she belonged to the Federation of Toushu Army, and the reason she left the military was to continue treating Eureka. She is always calm and has rich life experience, so aside from being a doctor, she often plays the role of a counselor. However, she herself denies this. She was once married to Dr. Bear. Even now he continues to love her, and he used to call her 'Little Bear-chan'.",
        372: "Gonjii is an old man living on the Gekko-Goh whose purpose, identity, and age are all unknown - a man of many mysteries. He appears and disappears unpredictably throughout the ship, always asking, 'Would you like some tea?' His fortune-telling boasts a considerable accuracy rate, and he is regarded with respect by the members of Gekkostate. In the final episode, it is revealed that he is actually a human-type Coralian like Eureka. Smiling contentedly at the years spent with Gekkostate, he vanished like mist.",
        373: "Maeter is one of the trio of orphans on the Gekko-Goh. She is 4 years old. She has a strong competitive spirit and is a precocious child. She adores Eureka, calling her 'Mama', and viewed Renton, who suddenly appeared and approached Eureka, with hostility. However, as she saw Renton's earnestness, her guard lowered, and eventually she warmed up to him. Her real parents were killed by Eureka's hand, and Eureka picked up and raised the three survivors.",
        374: "One of the three orphans on the Gekko-Goh. Three years old. Because he is the youngest, he is quite spoiled. He called Eureka 'Mama' and adored her, and viewed Renton, who appeared suddenly and approached Eureka, with hostility. However, as Renton's earnestness wore down his guard, he eventually opened up to him. His real parents were killed by Eureka's hand, and Eureka picked up and raised the three survivors.",
        375: "One of the three orphans on the Gekko-Goh. Five years old. He speaks little and is very shy with strangers, but sometimes shows the drive and self-reliance expected of the oldest. He called Eureka 'Mama' and adored her, and viewed Renton, who appeared suddenly and approached Eureka, with hostility. However, as Renton's earnestness wore down his guard, he eventually opened up to him. His real parents were killed by Eureka's hand, and Eureka picked up and raised the three survivors.",
        376: "Renton's grandfather. A craftsman-like old man whose stubbornness shows on his face. He is full of human warmth - he genuinely worries about his grandson, rages at the military for covering up the fact of his son's death, and shows kindness to young children. He is apparently a well-known figure among diggers, and in that circle is more famous than the hero Adroc. He demonstrated the family technique of 'tuning machines to be peaky', which he passed on to his grandson, and left Dominic groaning after repairing his motorcycle. In truth, he was once a mechanic belonging to Trezor Technical Institute. When the Nirvash Spec 2 required a lift board, he poured all his effort into building it, and while surrounded by the military, sent the board flying along a ley line. In the epilogue, after Renton and Eureka were gone, he took in the three orphans, Maurice and the others.",
        378: "Renton's older sister. She vanished several years ago and has been missing ever since. Later, Holland revealed that Scub Coral was involved in her disappearance and that it was connected to their own past. During the story, Renton's monologue of 'Sis...' was inserted at every turn. Because she had served as a substitute mother to him, it was thought he had not been able to let go of her. But from the middle of the story onward, this ceased, and as a result it suggested Renton's mental growth.",
        379: "The captain who leads the Izumo unit in the Federation of the Tower State's military. Stubborn and foul-mouthed, but a true soldier who approaches his duties with integrity. He did not take a liking to Dominic, who came aboard his ship as an observer. He frequently encountered the Gekko-Goh during attempts to capture the Nirvash TypeZERO and during Coralian surveys, and they fought fierce battles, but no conclusion was reached. After witnessing human experimentation alongside Dominic at the Novak Foundation's medical facility and reading the article in 'ray=out', he began to question the status quo. In the end, he left the military and, together with Gekkostate, faced what could be called a reckless battle.",
        380: "Dominic Soreil is a soldier belonging to the Intelligence Section 7 of the Federation of Toushuu. His rank is lieutenant. He is 20 years old. Basically, he is a capable young man, having reached the rank of lieutenant officer at a young age. However, contrary to his appearance, he is stubborn and hot-tempered, and he has many shortcomings that make him seem hardly like a soldier, such as being severely directionally challenged and unable to read maps, and vomiting at the sight of corpses. He serves as Anemone's caretaker, managing her through instructions and medication, while secretly harboring feelings of love for her. He had long been devoted to Dewey, and assisted him as a trusted subordinate. Even while Dewey was imprisoned, he continued to contact him without minding being relegated to a sinecure, and eventually returned to the military mainstream along with Dewey. However, seeing Dewey's methods of placing importance on children like the Ageha Squad, he gradually began to question Dewey's ways. In the end, he resolved to defect from the military for Anemone's sake, and displayed his passionate nature by making declarations called 'idiot' in front of the Gekkostate members, and by charging alone into the Scab Coral for Anemone. He then succeeded in rescuing her and winning her heart.",
        381: "Dewey Novak was a soldier belonging to the Intelligence Department of the Federation of Toushuu military. His rank was lieutenant colonel. He was 36 years old. At first glance, he appeared gentle and quiet, but the cruelty and ambition hidden beneath were immeasurable. He was long confined, taking responsibility for the incident of Holland leaving the military. However, with the occurrence of the Seven Swell phenomenon, he was released by the Three Sages and promoted to colonel. He took command of the entire military and began to act in order to carry out the 'Ageha Plan' advocated by Adroc. He steadily advanced his plans, organizing the Ageha Squad as his pawns and taming Anemone. However, his younger brother and sworn enemy Holland and Gekkostate became obstacles, leading to repeated clashes and conflicts. In the end, the brothers fought a bare-handed death match, but the bullet that ended his life was one he had fired himself.",
        382: "Anemone is a girl belonging to the Federation of Toushuu military who pilots the Nirvash type the END. She keeps Gulliver, a mysterious creature whose thoughts are unknowable, as a pet. Her emotions fluctuate wildly, and she is extremely selfish and capricious. She constantly gave trouble to Dominic, her caretaker, but gradually her attitude softened, and a clear change in her feelings could be seen. In contrast, the goodwill she initially held toward Dewey gradually transformed into disgust. While suppressing the unbearable headaches that frequently visited her with medication, she repeatedly fought against Eureka and Renton. In the final battle at the great hole opened in the Tenshan Mountains, she attacked the Nirvash as if throwing everything away. But at the calls of Eureka and Renton, who responded to the Nirvash's voice, and furthermore the voice of Dominic who rushed there, she finally stopped fighting. Immediately after, Dominic was thrown out of the small boat, but what connected the reaching hands of Anemone and Dominic in midair was none other than Gulliver.",
        383: "Charles Beams is a courier who flies around the world in the Hakuchou-Gou with his beloved wife, Ray. He has a generous and chivalrous personality, and when he happened to meet Renton, who had run away from home, they hit it off, and he treated him like his own son. For a time, he even tried to make Renton his adopted son, but when Renton casually uttered the word 'Gekko-Goh', their time as a family came to an end. His true identity is a freelancer belonging to an mobile strike unit of the Federation of Toushuu military. Furthermore, he was an old acquaintance of Holland with whom he had long ago parted ways. He encouraged Renton and sent him back, and with complicated feelings, he led the military in an attack on the Gekko-Goh, but it failed. The second time, he and Ray alone launched a close-quarters battle, engaging Holland in a fierce fight, but he was distracted by the Nirvash, caught off guard, and fell after taking a large amount of gunfire to the abdomen.",
        384: "Ray Beams is a courier who flies around the world in the Hakuchou-Gou with her beloved husband, Charles. She is a warm-hearted woman, and her cooking is a point of pride for Charles. She doted on Renton, who had run away from home and whom they happened to meet, as if he were her own son. Ray, whose body could not bear children, at one time even considered making Renton her adopted son. But when Renton casually uttered the word 'Eureka', their time as a family came to an end. Her true identity is a freelancer belonging to an mobile strike unit of the Federation of Toushuu military. Furthermore, she believed that Eureka was the cause of her inability to bear children, and harbored fierce hatred toward her. She encouraged Renton and sent him off, and attacked the Gekko-Goh with the military, but it failed. The second time, she and Charles alone launched a close-quarters battle, but she lost Charles in a gunfight with Holland. At the very end, she used two Spearheads as decoys under autopilot and attempted a suicide attack with the Hakuchou-Gou, but she was no match for Gekkostate's coordination and followed Charles in death.",
        385: "Greg Bear Egan was a leading researcher of Archetype studies who advocated the theory that the Scab Coral were an intelligent life form. Despite his massive build and Mohawk hairstyle, he had a gentle personality contrary to his name, and sweets were his favorite food. He was commonly known by the nickname 'Doctor Bear.' He had a past in which he was once married to Misha, and when he revealed this fact, everyone around him was astonished.",
        386: "Morita was the director of the Trezor Technical Research Institute, a research facility under the direct control of the Tower State Federation military. Despite his position as a military officer, he had a fateful personality in that he could not suppress his impulses as a researcher whenever he encountered an interesting research subject. He was involved in the modification of the Nirvash to its Spec 2 form and in the conversion of the Jurgens squad's Izumo ship into the Super Izumo, and he spared no effort or cooperation for the sake of his research.",
        387: 'Tiptree was a follower of Vodarac. He was a wanted person pursued by the Tower State Federation military, was taken under the protection of Gekkostate, and headed for the holy land. He later appeared again when Eureka and the others infiltrated Vodara Palace, the headquarters of Vodarac, and assisted them.',
        388: 'Norbu was a high priest of Vodarac. He was the one who had once taught Holland the truth of this world and gave him the impetus to found Gekkostate. However, he was a corrupt priest whose strange and worldly behavior stood out, such as hating baths, dearly loving mayonnaise, and suddenly making the members of Gekkostate play soccer. A Compac Drive was embedded in his chest, granting him mysterious powers. That was a vestige of when he had attempted to break through the Zone with Sakuya, a humanoid Coralian, in the past.',
        389: 'Sakuya was a humanoid Coralian discovered before Eureka, venerated as a saint by the Vodarac faithful. She had once fallen in love with Norbu, her caretaker, and together they attempted to enter the Zone, but failed, and she became Compac. Thereafter, she protected Vodara Palace with a barrier for some forty years. To enable Eureka and Renton to break through the Great Wall, she and Norbu together raised a Pororokka, and a Zone linking to the true promised land was born.',
        391: "Gulliver was Anemone's pet. Against those he disliked, he exercised a special ability (?) of increasing his weight and pinning them down. His victims were almost always Dominic. Since his expression never changed, it was impossible to tell what he was thinking. However, he loved Anemone dearly, and as her feelings toward Dominic began to change, he no longer became heavy. In the final battle at the Tenshan Mountains, he played a crucial role by holding together the two falling people and saving them.",
        394: "Coda was one of the three sages who made up the Council of Sages, the de facto rulers of the Pledgio Tower State Federation. He held strong influence over the federation's military as well. Having been drawn in by Dewey, he betrayed the Council of Sages and transferred all his power to Dewey.",
        395: "Kuzemi was one of the three sages who made up the Council of Sages, the de facto rulers of the Pledgio Tower State Federation. He held strong influence over the federation's military as well. He was shot dead by Dewey when Dewey staged his coup.",
        396: "Buraya was one of the three sages who made up the Council of Sages, the de facto rulers of the Pledgio Tower State Federation. He held strong influence over the federation's military as well. He was killed when Dewey staged his coup.",
        403: "Eidel Bernal was a major general in the New Earth Federation military. She was a capable officer who had been promoted to major general in recognition of her achievements in establishing the UN. She had a gentle and thoughtful personality, worried about the future of the multi-dimensional world, and commanded many followers within the military. She sought to reform the corrupt upper echelons from within, and to that end she moved her direct special operations unit, the Kaimera, to secretly support various organizations and individuals. She maintained a refined demeanor and never lost her Madonna-like smile, though she could sometimes act impulsively to stop Dr. Jey's rampage. However, these were merely her surface traits; in truth, she was an egotist who looked down on others and believed herself the most fit to rule the world. Her true nature was that of an artificial human created by Ji Eidel Bernal, and every action she took was predetermined by Ji Eidel.",
        404: "A brigadier general of the New Earth Federation Forces. She began actions to bring the entire world under her control, aiming to become the 'ruler of the new world.' Her true identity is an artificial human created by Ji Eder Bernard to satisfy his own desires. Everything about her, from her appearance and personality to her thoughts and hobbies, was set by Ji Eder. Ji Eder installed the 'Bind Spell,' an activation key for absolute obedience, into Eder, and through it he controlled her actions while in the form of Jee. Eder did not know she was an artificial human until her final moments, and when she learned the truth, she completely lost her reason and fell into a state of rampage.",
        405: "The true form of Doctor Jee, and the man who created the artificial human Eder Bernard. The name Ji Eder Bernard is also a convenient alias; his real name exists separately. He has succeeded in the limited control of the power of origin (Origin Law), and uses that power to act as his desires dictate. His principle of action is the single phrase, 'If it's interesting, it's good!' and he enjoys the existence of the multi-dimensional world born from the temporal oscillation warheads more than anyone else. Through the application of the power of origin, he integrates the abilities of multiple selves existing between parallel worlds, surpassing ordinary humans in every respect. He is also freed from concepts such as ethics and morality, and is driven by desires that others find difficult to understand, making his intentions and actions hard to read. The process by which he unraveled the power of origin remains shrouded in mystery.",
        406: 'An elderly scientist serving Eder Bernard. His specialties are mechanical engineering and temporal control technology, and he develops mobile weapons for Kaimera. He always overwhelms those around him with his high tension, and he greatly adores Brigadier General Eder. His true identity is the Black Charisma, Ji Eder Bernard, the creator of the artificial human Eder Bernard. For his own pleasure, Ji Eder deliberately took the form of Jee and served under Eder.',
        407: "A soldier of the New Earth Federation Forces. He is the captain of the Kaimera First Unit under Eder's direct command, with the rank of captain. He is close friends with Captain Shuran of the Kaimera Second Unit. He believes in Eder Bernard's ideals and fights to reform the New Earth Federation Forces and establish order in the multi-dimensional world. During infiltration operations, he feigns the persona of a earnest and pure good young man to put opponents off guard. However, his true personality is hysterical and self-centered, and he goes beyond having a phobia to actually hate the existence of women. The sole exception to his misogyny is Eder, and he openly declares that he would give even his life for her sake.",
        408: "A soldier of the New Earth Federation Forces. He is the captain of the Kaimera Second Unit under Eder's direct command, with the rank of captain. He demonstrates his true worth in rear-area missions such as maintaining public order and information warfare. He enjoys watching situations fall into chaos due to his own plans and openly states this, showing a malicious side. His calm composure and cool demeanor in any situation give others a cold impression, but that is a pose to hide his inner anxiety. He himself wishes to live by his emotions, and for that reason he both hates and is strongly drawn to the impetuous Raven.",
        409: "Tsuine Espio is a military officer of the New Earth Federation Army. As captain of the Kaiymera Third Platoon directly under Edel, she also served as the liaison between Kaiymera and Asakim, accompanying him in his activities. Having been present at the detonation of the time-space oscillation bomb, she lost her subordinates in the resulting displacement and was condemned to a harsh life across the multi-dimensional worlds. For this reason, she hated chaos and took part in Edel's plan to govern Earth, while also serving Ji-Edel as a free existence who could rescue her from her trauma. However, she could not keep up with his extreme personality and gradually found herself drawn to Asakim.",
        410: "Asakim Dowin is a young man who, having committed a great sin in the past and being forbidden even to die, wanders through various times and spaces together with Shurouga. To escape this fate, he wishes to obtain the power of the Taiji, and he himself participates in the battles among the owners of the Spheres, which are fragments of the Taiji's will.",
    },
}
